WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.040
Imagine for a second that you are a medieval scribe.

00:03.120 --> 00:05.380
Oh, setting the scene right away. I like it.

00:05.460 --> 00:06.840
Yeah, I want you to really picture it.

00:06.940 --> 00:10.220
You're sitting at this slanted wooden desk.

00:10.360 --> 00:11.800
It's lit by candlelight.

00:12.080 --> 00:14.720
And you are holding this incredibly expensive,

00:15.360 --> 00:18.920
meticulously prepared piece of animal skin.

00:20.320 --> 00:20.880
Parchment.

00:21.040 --> 00:23.220
Right, which you cannot afford to mess up.

00:23.420 --> 00:25.320
Exactly. You cannot make a mistake.

00:25.320 --> 00:29.780
And you are trying to write down this crucial word.

00:29.920 --> 00:32.920
Maybe it's a legal decree or, you know, a piece of sacred text.

00:33.220 --> 00:36.860
But the writing system you are forced to use is fundamentally,

00:37.260 --> 00:38.100
well, it's just ambiguous.

00:38.440 --> 00:39.120
Extremely ambiguous.

00:39.440 --> 00:42.100
Right, because half the letters look completely identical to each other.

00:42.340 --> 00:45.660
So when you draw this single sweeping curve on a page,

00:45.800 --> 00:48.740
it could mean a D sound or it could mean a DH sound.

00:48.900 --> 00:51.000
And the reader later on will just, I mean,

00:51.580 --> 00:53.540
they'll just have to guess based on the context.

00:53.540 --> 00:56.340
Which is a terrible system for preserving important information.

00:56.800 --> 00:57.080
Exactly.

00:58.080 --> 01:00.960
So as this scribe, you obviously want to fix this ambiguity.

01:02.120 --> 01:03.100
But you have two choices.

01:03.440 --> 01:08.800
Do you simply add a tiny dot above the curve to clarify which letter it is?

01:09.160 --> 01:13.600
Or do you invent a completely new sweeping architectural rule

01:13.600 --> 01:16.320
for how every single letter in the entire alphabet

01:16.320 --> 01:18.340
physically connects to every other letter?

01:18.660 --> 01:20.180
Seems like an extreme choice.

01:20.240 --> 01:20.480
Right.

01:20.480 --> 01:24.200
On the surface, you'd probably think, well, those are just two different ways to solve a problem.

01:24.360 --> 01:28.060
Like two different sizes of the same basic task of, you know, writing.

01:28.800 --> 01:32.820
But what if I told you that one of those choices is just a simple edit to a document?

01:33.320 --> 01:35.140
And the other choice is something else entirely.

01:35.400 --> 01:35.560
Yeah.

01:35.840 --> 01:39.080
The other choice actually rewrites the physical boundaries of reality

01:39.080 --> 01:41.020
for that language until the end of time.

01:41.240 --> 01:42.220
That is quite the hook.

01:42.400 --> 01:45.420
Well, welcome to this custom-tailored deep dive into the source material.

01:45.420 --> 01:49.160
We are unpacking an absolutely fascinating academic paper today.

01:49.260 --> 01:52.980
It was published in August 2026 by the researcher Flyxion.

01:53.940 --> 01:55.920
And it is titled, let me get this right,

01:56.080 --> 01:57.220
Depth Before Derivation,

01:58.000 --> 02:01.760
Metal Level Modification in Orthographic and Morphological Stabilization.

02:02.080 --> 02:05.620
Which is a very dense title for an incredibly profound concept.

02:05.740 --> 02:06.600
Yeah, it's a mouthful.

02:06.600 --> 02:13.160
But our mission today is basically to completely upend how you think about complex systems.

02:13.500 --> 02:17.000
Because for a long time, the dominant theory out there,

02:17.660 --> 02:19.740
this model called embodied constraint,

02:20.380 --> 02:26.060
it argued that human writing systems evolve purely based on a flat cost-benefit analysis.

02:26.400 --> 02:28.720
Right, treating language like a simple ledger book.

02:28.800 --> 02:30.320
Exactly, like an accounting problem.

02:30.740 --> 02:33.240
You weigh the physical effort it takes to write a symbol

02:33.240 --> 02:36.000
against how clearly it can be read by someone else.

02:36.000 --> 02:39.960
And if the benefit outweighs the cost, boom, the change sticks.

02:40.380 --> 02:43.240
But Flyxion's paper argues this view is entirely flat.

02:43.380 --> 02:45.420
It's missing a completely hidden dimension.

02:45.600 --> 02:46.360
A crucial dimension.

02:46.480 --> 02:46.840
Exactly.

02:47.020 --> 02:50.280
If you actually want to understand why certain changes in a system just, you know,

02:51.020 --> 02:52.020
easily fade away,

02:52.340 --> 02:55.160
while others become these permanent irreversible laws,

02:55.640 --> 02:57.540
you have to look at the depth of the change.

02:57.840 --> 02:59.560
Not just the cost, but the depth.

02:59.720 --> 03:00.740
And to explore that,

03:01.260 --> 03:04.200
we are going to use a very specific historical laboratory today.

03:04.300 --> 03:04.500
Right.

03:04.760 --> 03:05.300
We are.

03:05.300 --> 03:08.940
The Arabic script and its underlying grammatical structure

03:08.940 --> 03:12.320
provides perhaps the most perfect historical laboratory

03:12.320 --> 03:15.480
to observe this hidden dimension in action.

03:15.980 --> 03:18.780
I mean, we are looking at a system that stabilized over centuries.

03:19.220 --> 03:24.980
It left behind this highly documented trail of how it solved massive informational bottlenecks.

03:24.980 --> 03:25.680
Oh, it's so cool.

03:25.680 --> 03:31.520
We're going to explore everything from, like, the microscopic placement of dots on individual letters

03:31.520 --> 03:35.660
all the way up to the sweeping mathematical architecture of Arabic verbs.

03:35.660 --> 03:38.980
It really is a masterclass in how systems lock into place.

03:39.220 --> 03:43.900
So by the end of this deep dive, you are going to have a completely new mental model

03:43.900 --> 03:48.420
for understanding how small tweaks differ fundamentally from systemic overhauls.

03:49.140 --> 03:52.920
And, you know, this framework, it doesn't just apply to ancient scribes or linguistics.

03:53.100 --> 03:53.580
Not at all.

03:53.620 --> 03:55.120
It applies to how you build habits, right?

03:55.560 --> 03:56.840
How companies design software.

03:57.360 --> 03:59.360
Even how we interact with artificial intelligence.

03:59.360 --> 04:02.720
It's universally applicable to any complex system.

04:03.000 --> 04:03.140
Yeah.

04:03.380 --> 04:07.080
So let's start by looking at that original theory, the embodied constraint model,

04:07.260 --> 04:11.740
just to understand why Flyxion felt the need to write this critique in the first place.

04:12.280 --> 04:17.240
Because the older model, it basically reduces the entire evolution of human writing

04:17.240 --> 04:19.620
down to a single mathematical equation, right?

04:19.680 --> 04:19.980
Right.

04:19.980 --> 04:24.740
It treats language stabilization as a pure equilibrium condition.

04:25.360 --> 04:30.440
The equation they present is S equals alpha D minus beta C.

04:30.740 --> 04:30.760
Okay.

04:30.900 --> 04:32.880
Let's break that down for people who aren't math majors.

04:33.000 --> 04:33.180
Sure.

04:33.600 --> 04:36.280
So in this framework, S represents stabilization.

04:37.220 --> 04:41.100
The theory posits that a writing system will basically settle into a stable state when

04:41.100 --> 04:42.820
it reaches a local maximum of S.

04:42.840 --> 04:44.460
So when things stop changing.

04:44.620 --> 04:45.000
Exactly.

04:45.320 --> 04:46.120
When it settles.

04:46.120 --> 04:50.160
Now, the two competing forces in this equation are D and C.

04:50.580 --> 04:52.060
D stands for distinctness.

04:52.180 --> 04:52.300
Okay.

04:52.360 --> 04:53.740
This is the informational game.

04:54.200 --> 04:58.640
When a scribe alters a letter to make it less ambiguous, like we talked about, the distinctness

04:58.640 --> 04:59.220
increases.

04:59.720 --> 05:04.520
The reader has an easier time distinguishing that specific word from another similar looking

05:04.520 --> 05:04.860
word.

05:04.960 --> 05:06.440
So distinctness is good.

05:06.740 --> 05:07.780
Distinctness is very good.

05:07.860 --> 05:08.600
But then you have C.

05:09.100 --> 05:10.280
C stands for cost.

05:10.540 --> 05:12.640
And this is the physical production cost.

05:12.640 --> 05:17.880
I mean, we are talking about the literal calories, the time, the motor control effort required

05:17.880 --> 05:21.160
for a human hand to produce that specific mark on the page.

05:21.620 --> 05:21.740
Right.

05:21.860 --> 05:23.760
Because writing by hand takes effort.

05:24.180 --> 05:24.460
Yes.

05:24.520 --> 05:25.360
Especially back then.

05:25.600 --> 05:26.160
Exactly.

05:26.640 --> 05:29.580
And it also includes the cognitive load of learning it.

05:29.920 --> 05:33.320
Then you have alpha and beta, which are simply these weighting parameters.

05:33.980 --> 05:39.820
They basically determine how much a specific society values clarity versus speed at any given

05:39.820 --> 05:40.740
historical moment.

05:40.740 --> 05:41.180
Okay.

05:41.680 --> 05:45.040
So I want to visualize this as like an old-fashioned balance scale.

05:45.120 --> 05:46.080
That's a good way to look at it.

05:46.300 --> 05:48.900
On one side, you have the clarity of the text, distinctness.

05:48.980 --> 05:52.860
On the other side, you have the hand-cramping effort of writing it, the cost.

05:53.380 --> 05:59.680
So if a scribe invents a new flourish on a letter that makes it incredibly distinct, but

05:59.680 --> 06:04.960
it takes like 10 extra seconds to draw, the system eventually rejects it because the cost

06:04.960 --> 06:05.740
is just too high.

06:06.060 --> 06:06.420
Exactly.

06:06.640 --> 06:07.820
The scribes will just stop doing it.

06:07.820 --> 06:14.020
But if a scribe finds a super lazy shortcut that saves a ton of time, but makes the text

06:14.020 --> 06:20.080
completely unreadable, the system also rejects that because the distinctness dropped way

06:20.080 --> 06:20.640
too low.

06:20.760 --> 06:20.980
Right.

06:21.100 --> 06:23.880
The readers will complain that they can't decipher the texts anymore.

06:23.880 --> 06:28.860
So the system only stabilizes when a modification is cheap enough to produce, but clear enough

06:28.860 --> 06:29.360
to read.

06:30.220 --> 06:34.340
It's a pure economic trade-off applied directly to the individual shapes on the page.

06:34.720 --> 06:34.920
Yeah.

06:35.000 --> 06:37.600
It relies on this principle of compression under constraint.

06:38.260 --> 06:43.480
And the embodied constraint model takes this economic dynamic and applies it uniformly to

06:43.480 --> 06:47.140
every single stabilizing event in the history of a script.

06:47.140 --> 06:48.800
Like a one-size-fits-all rule.

06:48.860 --> 06:49.300
Exactly.

06:49.580 --> 06:54.300
It evaluates every single modification through this exact same flat lens.

06:55.160 --> 06:58.380
Now, Flyxion acknowledges that this dynamic absolutely exists.

06:58.540 --> 07:01.940
I mean, scribes were indeed trying to balance effort and clarity.

07:02.140 --> 07:03.320
They weren't ignoring the real world.

07:03.600 --> 07:03.840
Right.

07:04.440 --> 07:09.840
But their critique, the core argument of this paper, is that this model collapses operations

07:09.840 --> 07:12.100
that act on completely different targets.

07:12.100 --> 07:18.660
The embodied constraint theory treats adding a single dot to a single letter and fundamentally

07:18.660 --> 07:24.120
changing the entire systemic rule for how a cursive alphabet connects as the exact same

07:24.120 --> 07:25.020
type of transaction.

07:25.020 --> 07:30.700
Because the mathematical formula, the S equals D minus C thing, it only has room for two questions.

07:30.880 --> 07:32.280
How much did this change cost?

07:32.380 --> 07:34.120
And how much clarity did it add?

07:34.240 --> 07:34.600
Yes.

07:34.680 --> 07:39.540
It just puts every change on a single sliding scale of magnitude, which is wild when you really

07:39.540 --> 07:40.140
think about it.

07:40.200 --> 07:40.600
It is.

07:40.600 --> 07:43.280
It misses the architecture of the system entirely.

07:43.460 --> 07:43.600
Okay.

07:43.680 --> 07:45.220
Let's test this with a software analogy.

07:45.480 --> 07:49.440
Because when I was reading this academic phrasing in the source material, it made me realize

07:49.440 --> 07:53.140
how strange that flat perspective actually is in practice.

07:53.600 --> 07:56.520
So imagine I am typing a document in Microsoft Word.

07:56.700 --> 07:56.920
Okay.

07:57.000 --> 07:57.620
Tracking with you.

07:57.820 --> 08:00.760
If I notice I misspelled a word, I just hit the backspace key, right?

08:00.840 --> 08:01.560
And I fix the typo.

08:01.640 --> 08:06.320
I just hit a tiny bit of cost, moving my finger to gain a tiny bit of distinctness, fixing

08:06.320 --> 08:06.760
the error.

08:06.900 --> 08:07.160
Right.

08:07.500 --> 08:08.360
A minor adjustment.

08:08.360 --> 08:15.020
Now, imagine an engineer at Microsoft decides to rewrite the entire underlying code of the

08:15.020 --> 08:16.040
Windows operating system.

08:16.060 --> 08:17.200
A massive undertaking.

08:17.420 --> 08:17.760
Exactly.

08:18.180 --> 08:22.740
But the flat model looks at both of these events and says, well, they both involve typing

08:22.740 --> 08:24.900
on a keyboard to improve a digital product.

08:25.080 --> 08:28.200
So one is just a much, much bigger version of the other.

08:28.300 --> 08:32.260
It treats rewriting an operating system as just a massive typo correction.

08:32.260 --> 08:32.860
Yes.

08:33.520 --> 08:38.740
But fundamentally, I mean, we know that one action edits the content inside a system, while

08:38.740 --> 08:43.100
the other action edits the actual rules of how content can even exist in the first place.

08:43.260 --> 08:43.500
Right.

08:43.780 --> 08:48.260
And that is exactly where Flyxion's paper steps in to formalize this distinction.

08:48.860 --> 08:54.660
They also introduces what they call the admissibility dynamics framework and this new conceptual axis

08:54.660 --> 08:56.480
called meta-depth K.

08:56.600 --> 08:57.560
Meta-depth K.

08:57.640 --> 08:57.820
Okay.

08:57.920 --> 08:58.400
Lay it on me.

08:58.400 --> 09:03.500
So to escape that flat ledger book we've been talking about, we have to classify modifications

09:03.500 --> 09:06.140
not by how much effort they take, but by their depth.

09:06.260 --> 09:06.540
Okay.

09:06.540 --> 09:13.320
A depth zero modification, which Flyxion denotes as M0, acts directly on the set of currently

09:13.320 --> 09:14.420
permitted configurations.

09:14.920 --> 09:18.300
It operates strictly within the existing admissibility structure.

09:18.300 --> 09:18.860
Okay.

09:18.980 --> 09:24.360
So going back to my software analogy, depth zero is just me adding a new word to my Word

09:24.360 --> 09:24.740
document.

09:25.400 --> 09:27.940
I am not changing how Microsoft Word functions at all.

09:28.160 --> 09:32.120
I am just using the existing rules to add a new item to my inventory.

09:32.260 --> 09:32.600
Exactly.

09:32.880 --> 09:37.620
You are inserting a fully specified object into a space that already knows how to receive

09:37.620 --> 09:37.860
it.

09:38.000 --> 09:39.740
It's a surface level addition.

09:40.040 --> 09:40.440
Got it.

09:40.680 --> 09:42.100
Depth zero is the surface.

09:42.100 --> 09:44.640
But then we take a recursive step upward.

09:45.340 --> 09:51.540
A depth one modification, M1, acts on the machinery that actually generates those configurations.

09:51.880 --> 09:52.200
Oh, okay.

09:52.320 --> 09:54.420
It does not act on the inventory of items.

09:54.600 --> 09:56.320
It acts on the rules governing the inventory.

09:56.740 --> 10:00.760
It changes the foundational parameter of what is even considered an admissible object in

10:00.760 --> 10:01.420
the first place.

10:01.500 --> 10:04.420
So that's the software engineer completely rewriting the operating system.

10:04.700 --> 10:05.220
Precisely.

10:05.500 --> 10:06.580
You aren't adding a file.

10:06.840 --> 10:09.080
You're changing how the hard drive stores data.

10:09.640 --> 10:11.100
And the depth axis is inductive.

10:11.100 --> 10:16.280
You can theoretically have depth two modifications that change the rules for how rules are made

10:16.280 --> 10:16.760
and so on.

10:16.960 --> 10:18.140
It's just turtles all the way down.

10:18.340 --> 10:18.580
Right.

10:18.900 --> 10:23.900
But the crucial failure of the flat model was its total blindness to this axis altogether.

10:24.300 --> 10:29.120
It just measured the ink on the page without ever asking whether that ink represented a

10:29.120 --> 10:33.080
depth zero insertion or a depth one architectural overhaul.

10:33.260 --> 10:33.520
Okay.

10:33.680 --> 10:37.960
So let's bring this out of the abstract math and into the physical history of the Arabic

10:37.960 --> 10:39.940
script because I think that makes it so much clearer.

10:39.940 --> 10:45.940
The paper uses this brilliant historical comparison to show the difference between depth zero dots

10:45.940 --> 10:47.720
and depth one rules.

10:47.840 --> 10:49.280
It's a fantastic comparison.

10:49.480 --> 10:50.320
Let's start with the dots.

10:50.340 --> 10:55.180
Because we mentioned earlier that before the Arabic alphabet adopted systematic dotting,

10:55.860 --> 10:58.540
several letters shared an identical skeletal base.

10:58.540 --> 11:04.820
The paper uses the example of the letter DAL representing the D sound and the letter DAL representing

11:04.820 --> 11:05.700
the DH sound.

11:06.480 --> 11:08.840
Back then, they were visually indistinguishable.

11:09.440 --> 11:14.720
They were both just a simple unadorned curve resting on the baseline, like a backward C shape.

11:14.800 --> 11:15.220
Exactly.

11:15.680 --> 11:20.660
A reader encountering that unadorned curve had to rely entirely on context to know which phone

11:20.660 --> 11:21.880
to actually produce.

11:22.260 --> 11:23.820
Was the word supposed to mean this or that?

11:23.860 --> 11:24.740
It must have been exhausting.

11:24.740 --> 11:26.360
It was highly ambiguous.

11:26.680 --> 11:30.420
So the modification introduced to solve this was dotting.

11:31.120 --> 11:36.440
A scribe simply placed a single dot above the curve to permanently differentiate DAL from

11:36.440 --> 11:36.860
DAL.

11:37.180 --> 11:39.300
And boom, ambiguity solved.

11:39.340 --> 11:40.280
Ambiguity solved.

11:40.280 --> 11:46.320
But if we analyze this through the admissibility dynamics framework, dotting is the quintessential

11:46.320 --> 11:47.780
depth zero operation.

11:48.720 --> 11:52.720
The modification introduces an augmentation to an existing skeletal base.

11:52.960 --> 11:59.160
It just reads the current state of the graph theme inventory, identifies a point of ambiguity, and writes one new

11:59.160 --> 12:01.280
admissible form into that inventory.

12:01.500 --> 12:03.300
It's a pure write operation.

12:03.540 --> 12:03.720
Yes.

12:04.000 --> 12:06.980
And to me, the most important part of this is what the dot doesn't do.

12:06.980 --> 12:12.140
I mean, adding that dot leaves every other rule of the writing system completely untouched,

12:12.240 --> 12:12.400
right?

12:12.440 --> 12:13.240
Completely untouched.

12:13.260 --> 12:16.280
It doesn't change how the letter DAL connects to the letter before it.

12:16.340 --> 12:18.260
It doesn't change how it connects to the letter after it.

12:18.420 --> 12:23.320
The whole generative machinery that powers the alphabet remains exactly as it was.

12:23.400 --> 12:24.000
That's the key.

12:24.000 --> 12:29.500
So even if, like, a central authority ordered the scribes to dot the entire alphabet overnight,

12:30.020 --> 12:36.220
resolving every single ambiguity in the entire language all at once, it would still be a

12:36.220 --> 12:37.060
depth zero change.

12:37.120 --> 12:37.580
Exactly.

12:38.020 --> 12:41.440
The sheer volume of dots added does not elevate the depth.

12:41.860 --> 12:47.480
You can execute a million depth zero writes, and they remain depth zero, because the underlying

12:47.480 --> 12:49.660
rules of generation are unaltered.

12:50.060 --> 12:51.720
Volume doesn't equal depth.

12:51.720 --> 12:53.300
Okay, that makes perfect sense.

12:53.380 --> 12:55.140
That is a surface-level modification.

12:55.280 --> 12:58.140
Now, we need to look at Flyxion's counterexample, because this is where it gets crazy.

12:58.540 --> 13:01.160
This historical event called positional regularization.

13:01.320 --> 13:01.560
Yes.

13:01.680 --> 13:06.840
This is a true depth one change, and the mechanics of how it works are just, well, they're mind-bending.

13:07.040 --> 13:08.820
Because Arabic is a cursive script, right?

13:09.220 --> 13:11.580
Letters physically connect to one another on the page.

13:12.040 --> 13:16.240
But before the rules stabilized into what we know today, the shape a letter took was highly

13:16.240 --> 13:16.600
fluid.

13:17.000 --> 13:17.700
Incredibly fluid.

13:17.700 --> 13:21.920
The shape of a letter depended entirely on its specific left and right neighbors.

13:22.300 --> 13:25.060
The paper expresses this as a combinatorial function.

13:25.200 --> 13:25.900
Let's hear the math.

13:25.980 --> 13:31.280
It's formalized as f given g sub i minus one, and g sub i plus one.

13:31.500 --> 13:31.980
Okay, hold on.

13:32.040 --> 13:33.560
Let me stop you there to visualize this.

13:34.140 --> 13:39.000
You're saying that the physical shape I have to draw for the letter, say b, would look completely

13:39.000 --> 13:43.920
different if it was squeezed between an a and a c versus being squeezed between an x and a y.

13:43.920 --> 13:48.020
That is the reality of early, context-sensitive ligatures.

13:48.420 --> 13:53.980
The specific stroke used to exit the previous letter mathematically dictates the entry angle

13:53.980 --> 13:58.240
of the current letter, which in turn dictates the exit angle into the subsequent letter.

13:58.280 --> 13:58.880
Oh my god.

13:59.060 --> 14:03.040
Give me a sense of the scale here, because they call it a combinatorial explosion, which

14:03.040 --> 14:03.660
sounds heavy.

14:04.060 --> 14:08.400
But if I only have 28 letters in an alphabet, how bad can the memorization really be?

14:08.520 --> 14:09.400
Well, let's do the math.

14:09.400 --> 14:14.720
If every letter connects uniquely to every other letter, you multiply 28 by 28 for just

14:14.720 --> 14:15.840
a two-letter combination.

14:16.580 --> 14:19.820
That yields nearly 800 unique joining shapes.

14:19.960 --> 14:20.200
800.

14:20.620 --> 14:21.480
And that's just two letters.

14:22.120 --> 14:25.100
Now factor in the third letter to complete the localized context.

14:25.460 --> 14:27.860
The domain of that function grows exponentially.

14:28.280 --> 14:34.520
So scribes were not just memorizing 28 letters, they were memorizing a massive, unbounded matrix

14:34.520 --> 14:37.260
of highly specific localized ligatures.

14:37.260 --> 14:40.340
That is a staggering cognitive load.

14:40.480 --> 14:44.900
I can't even imagine trying to learn that as a kid, let alone standardizing it across

14:44.900 --> 14:45.940
a massive empire.

14:46.200 --> 14:51.000
It's essentially unscalable, which is why the historical regularization process happened.

14:51.180 --> 14:55.040
And what it did was fundamentally destroy this context-sensitive matrix.

14:55.300 --> 15:01.580
It replaced that massive, unbounded function with a rigid, thick system known as the four-position

15:01.580 --> 15:02.080
rule.

15:02.200 --> 15:03.200
The four-position rule.

15:03.280 --> 15:03.500
Okay.

15:03.600 --> 15:04.300
How does that work?

15:04.300 --> 15:08.580
From that point on, a letter could only ever take a maximum of four forms.

15:09.520 --> 15:11.600
Isolated, initial, medial, and final.

15:11.980 --> 15:17.060
Wait, meaning it doesn't matter if the letter before it is an A, an X, or a Z. If the letter's

15:17.060 --> 15:19.240
in the middle of a word, it just takes the medial shape.

15:19.620 --> 15:19.920
Period.

15:19.920 --> 15:20.640
Exactly.

15:20.640 --> 15:25.700
The massive combinatorial function was destroyed and replaced by a lower complexity function,

15:25.900 --> 15:29.160
and we must ask why this constitutes a depth one change.

15:29.400 --> 15:29.420
Right.

15:29.580 --> 15:32.680
This regularization did not just add a new shape to the alphabet.

15:33.140 --> 15:37.820
It did not just resolve a visual ambiguity between two specific consonants, like a dot.

15:38.300 --> 15:42.100
It dismantled the old generative rule and installed a completely new one.

15:42.100 --> 15:45.320
The object being modified was not a grapheme on a page.

15:45.840 --> 15:50.900
The object being modified was the invisible mathematical machinery that generated the graphemes.

15:50.900 --> 15:51.340
Okay.

15:51.760 --> 15:56.880
But if I am an ancient scribe reading this paper over my shoulder, I might ask, you know,

15:57.040 --> 15:59.520
why does this conceptual difference even matter?

16:00.100 --> 16:02.940
I dotted a letter, and the word is easier to read.

16:03.400 --> 16:06.300
I use the new four-position rule, and the word is easier to read.

16:06.640 --> 16:09.380
The end result is just distinctness and clarity for both.

16:09.940 --> 16:13.040
Why do I need to care about whether it was depth zero or depth one?

16:13.360 --> 16:16.720
Because it dictates the future trajectory of the entire system.

16:16.960 --> 16:17.440
How so?

16:17.440 --> 16:24.120
When you introduce a depth zero change, like a dot, you solve one localized immediate problem.

16:24.820 --> 16:26.640
You have differentiated dull from dull.

16:27.120 --> 16:30.180
But when you introduce a depth one rule, like the four-position system,

16:30.440 --> 16:34.080
you literally dictate the future limits of reality for that language.

16:34.180 --> 16:34.580
Oh, I see.

16:34.860 --> 16:39.900
Once that rule locks into place, every single new letter, every single borrowed sound,

16:40.100 --> 16:45.760
every new word added to the vocabulary for the rest of history is forced to obey that four-position framework.

16:45.960 --> 16:47.400
That is so powerful.

16:47.880 --> 16:49.200
Think about the software update again.

16:49.600 --> 16:53.360
If a developer fixes a typo on a website, it helps the user today.

16:53.920 --> 16:57.320
But if the developer changes the fundamental architecture of the database,

16:57.900 --> 17:02.460
every single user, every piece of data, and every future feature built on that website

17:02.460 --> 17:05.340
has to run through that new architecture forever.

17:05.660 --> 17:06.140
Exactly.

17:06.600 --> 17:09.580
A depth zero change puts a new piece of furniture in the room.

17:09.900 --> 17:12.840
A depth one change rewrites the blueprints of the house.

17:13.460 --> 17:14.920
That is a perfect way to put it.

17:14.920 --> 17:21.440
And the flat cost-benefit model could not see this difference because it only knew how to measure the immediate cost of the ink

17:21.440 --> 17:23.960
and the immediate benefit of the reader's clarity.

17:23.960 --> 17:30.720
It lacked any mechanism to measure the historical structural weight of rewriting a generative rule.

17:30.720 --> 17:34.660
Which naturally forces us to look deeper into the architecture of the language itself.

17:34.920 --> 17:39.320
Because if the physical ink on the page has these distinct levels of depth, we have to ask,

17:39.320 --> 17:43.040
does the spoken grammar of the language follow the same in visible physics?

17:43.540 --> 17:44.880
Oh, this is where it gets really interesting.

17:45.020 --> 17:50.620
This takes us beyond the orthography, the writing system, and straight into the Arabic morphology.

17:50.820 --> 17:53.920
Basically, the generative engine of the words themselves.

17:54.180 --> 17:54.460
Right.

17:54.460 --> 18:01.760
Because according to Flyxion, the Arabic grammatical tradition intuitively understood this depth distinction

18:01.760 --> 18:06.320
centuries before modern linguistics had the, you know, the mathematical terminology for it.

18:06.580 --> 18:13.500
They understood that you could completely separate the raw material of meaning from the structural machinery that shapes it.

18:14.000 --> 18:18.880
And they demonstrated this using a generic fixed exemplar root.

18:18.880 --> 18:23.420
Yes. The traditional grammar models use the triconsonantal root, F-L-Q.

18:23.580 --> 18:24.200
F-L-Q.

18:24.360 --> 18:28.720
Exactly. Which forms the word Fala, meaning to do or to act.

18:29.300 --> 18:33.340
In Arabic morphology, the core semantic meaning, in this case the concept of action,

18:33.540 --> 18:35.360
is carried purely by the consonants.

18:35.460 --> 18:36.040
Just the skeleton.

18:36.220 --> 18:36.860
Just the skeleton.

18:37.140 --> 18:40.060
The grammatical structure, meaning the tense, the voice, the agency,

18:40.220 --> 18:43.640
all of that is provided by the vowels and a specific set of added letters.

18:44.200 --> 18:48.060
So the grammatical tradition takes this raw conceptual root of doing

18:48.060 --> 18:52.680
and runs it through a set of canonical templates known as the measures or azan.

18:53.120 --> 18:57.100
I really want to slowly walk through what it actually sounds and feels like

18:57.100 --> 18:58.920
to run a route through this machinery.

18:59.120 --> 19:01.160
Because honestly, when you read it,

19:01.480 --> 19:05.420
it is like watching a mathematical equation come to life in the human vocal tract.

19:05.480 --> 19:06.340
It really is elegant.

19:06.340 --> 19:09.960
The source material lists out 10 of these canonical forms.

19:10.460 --> 19:12.160
Forms I through X.

19:12.940 --> 19:14.260
So form I is the raw base.

19:14.260 --> 19:19.320
You take FLQ, you insert the standard short A vowels, and you get Fala.

19:19.920 --> 19:20.440
He did.

19:20.500 --> 19:21.500
The baseline action.

19:21.700 --> 19:23.640
Now form 2 takes that exact same root.

19:24.180 --> 19:27.340
But the template applies a very specific physical operation.

19:28.000 --> 19:29.600
It doubles the middle consonant.

19:29.940 --> 19:30.680
It geminates it.

19:31.000 --> 19:32.460
So Fala becomes Fala.

19:32.600 --> 19:32.860
Right.

19:33.000 --> 19:34.280
With a heavier middle sound.

19:34.360 --> 19:34.520
Yeah.

19:34.740 --> 19:36.260
And the core meaning of doing remains.

19:37.300 --> 19:40.560
But the template forces a shift in intensity or agency.

19:40.560 --> 19:44.800
It now means he made someone do or he did something intensely.

19:45.120 --> 19:49.840
The physical operation of doubling the consonant predictably alters the semantic output.

19:49.920 --> 19:50.580
It's like an algorithm.

19:50.960 --> 19:52.040
Then we move to form 3.

19:52.540 --> 19:54.040
This template doesn't double a consonant.

19:54.380 --> 19:55.920
It elongates the first vowel.

19:56.260 --> 19:57.360
So Fala because Fala.

19:57.700 --> 19:59.120
Suddenly the action becomes reciprocal.

19:59.660 --> 20:01.420
He did something with or against someone.

20:01.780 --> 20:02.960
Just by stretching a vowel.

20:03.120 --> 20:04.240
Just by stretching a vowel.

20:04.800 --> 20:07.260
Form 4 adds a specific prefix,

20:07.260 --> 20:09.300
a glottal stop called a Hamza,

20:09.720 --> 20:10.340
before the root.

20:10.860 --> 20:12.300
So Falala becomes a Fala.

20:12.840 --> 20:14.420
He caused something to be done.

20:14.740 --> 20:15.900
A shift in causality.

20:16.560 --> 20:17.880
And skipping ahead to form X,

20:18.120 --> 20:20.140
the template adds a complex prefix,

20:20.620 --> 20:20.820
ist.

20:21.360 --> 20:23.180
The word becomes istifala.

20:23.660 --> 20:24.780
He sought to have it done,

20:24.880 --> 20:26.340
or he asked for it to be done.

20:26.600 --> 20:29.440
So you basically take this raw semantic clay,

20:29.600 --> 20:31.620
you shove it into these different mechanical molds,

20:31.800 --> 20:34.820
and you get a perfectly predictable structural output.

20:34.820 --> 20:37.320
And every single one of these forms is generated

20:37.320 --> 20:39.980
from those exact same three bass consonants.

20:40.600 --> 20:42.780
The templates are created through composite operators,

20:43.180 --> 20:45.940
drawn from a strictly limited set of primitive moves.

20:46.200 --> 20:46.760
Like a toolkit.

20:47.000 --> 20:47.400
Exactly.

20:47.820 --> 20:48.480
Inserting a vowel,

20:48.760 --> 20:49.520
doubling a consonant,

20:50.080 --> 20:50.920
lengthening a vowel,

20:51.100 --> 20:53.300
or fixing specific elements like the Hamza,

20:53.460 --> 20:53.800
a Ta,

20:53.960 --> 20:54.500
or an Ist.

20:54.680 --> 20:55.660
So if I'm a speaker,

20:55.940 --> 20:56.800
and I take a root,

20:56.900 --> 20:58.380
and apply one of these templates to it,

20:58.520 --> 21:00.600
what level of depth am I operating on?

21:00.860 --> 21:02.680
Applying a known measure to a root

21:02.680 --> 21:05.060
is a pure depth zero operation.

21:05.520 --> 21:08.480
Imagine you encounter a completely novel root,

21:08.840 --> 21:09.960
a loan word perhaps,

21:10.120 --> 21:11.680
and you want to say that someone

21:11.680 --> 21:13.160
sought to have that thing done.

21:13.640 --> 21:15.660
You simply map the new root

21:15.660 --> 21:17.060
into the form X template.

21:17.460 --> 21:18.160
Just plug and play.

21:18.280 --> 21:18.480
Right.

21:18.700 --> 21:20.740
You are executing a pre-existing rule.

21:21.280 --> 21:22.920
It is a single write operation

21:22.920 --> 21:25.240
into the space of drivable forms.

21:25.460 --> 21:28.260
It leaves the rule itself totally unchanged.

21:28.260 --> 21:30.960
I think of this exactly like a metal baking mold.

21:31.580 --> 21:32.540
Taking a sheet of dough

21:32.540 --> 21:34.160
and using this star-shaped mold

21:34.160 --> 21:35.180
to stamp out a cookie

21:35.180 --> 21:37.780
is a depth zero execution, right?

21:37.960 --> 21:39.380
You can stamp out a thousand cookies,

21:39.580 --> 21:40.920
you can use chocolate chip dough,

21:41.080 --> 21:41.720
sugar cookie dough,

21:41.800 --> 21:43.380
completely new roots you've never heard before.

21:43.640 --> 21:46.220
But the physical action is just execution.

21:46.500 --> 21:46.760
Yes.

21:46.980 --> 21:47.360
However,

21:47.860 --> 21:48.740
the historical moment

21:48.740 --> 21:50.300
when an engineer actually designed

21:50.300 --> 21:52.060
that specific star-shaped mold,

21:52.540 --> 21:53.440
forged it in metal,

21:53.560 --> 21:56.000
and threw away the infinite other possible shapes

21:56.000 --> 21:56.680
they could have made.

21:56.680 --> 21:58.340
That is a depth one event.

21:58.620 --> 21:59.800
That is the perfect analogy.

22:00.100 --> 22:01.200
The measure set itself,

22:01.280 --> 22:02.400
the historical decision

22:02.400 --> 22:03.960
that there will be these 10

22:03.960 --> 22:05.940
or sometimes 15 canonical templates

22:05.940 --> 22:08.420
out of an infinite combinatorial universe

22:08.420 --> 22:09.520
of possible syllables.

22:09.720 --> 22:12.380
That is the depth one stabilization object.

22:12.700 --> 22:14.040
Because it didn't have to be that way, right?

22:14.380 --> 22:15.020
Not at all.

22:15.660 --> 22:16.260
In principle,

22:16.480 --> 22:17.880
human vocal tracts are capable

22:17.880 --> 22:19.380
of an unbounded space

22:19.380 --> 22:22.080
of random consonant and vowel recombinations.

22:22.820 --> 22:24.760
A language could theoretically allow

22:24.760 --> 22:26.740
literally any sequence of prefixes

22:26.740 --> 22:28.180
and internal vowel shifts

22:28.180 --> 22:29.080
to carry meaning.

22:29.080 --> 22:31.440
The language could have been absolute chaos.

22:31.680 --> 22:32.240
It could have been,

22:32.520 --> 22:33.700
but it locked it down.

22:33.880 --> 22:36.160
It reduced an unbounded generative space

22:36.160 --> 22:38.180
to a closed, finite,

22:38.360 --> 22:39.720
highly teachable set of rules.

22:40.040 --> 22:41.340
This historical stabilization

22:41.340 --> 22:42.900
is structurally identical

22:42.900 --> 22:44.680
to the positional regularization

22:44.680 --> 22:45.800
of the script we just talked about.

22:45.860 --> 22:46.360
Oh, wow.

22:46.520 --> 22:48.200
Yeah, the four position rule for writing.

22:48.340 --> 22:48.580
Yeah.

22:48.760 --> 22:50.340
And the 10 forms for speaking.

22:50.680 --> 22:51.080
Exactly.

22:51.600 --> 22:53.360
And this is where Flyxion highlights

22:53.360 --> 22:54.600
a critical observation

22:54.600 --> 22:57.300
made by the older embodied constraint model.

22:57.760 --> 22:59.440
An observation they actually made correctly,

22:59.660 --> 23:01.320
but they misdiagnosed fundamentally.

23:01.540 --> 23:02.480
Are you talking about the concept

23:02.480 --> 23:03.760
of predictive generativity?

23:04.100 --> 23:05.600
Yes, predictive generativity.

23:06.160 --> 23:07.960
The older model marveled

23:07.960 --> 23:09.620
at the efficiency of Arabic speakers.

23:10.340 --> 23:11.620
They observed that a speaker

23:11.620 --> 23:14.240
can hear an entirely unfamiliar root,

23:14.440 --> 23:16.180
and if it is presented in, say,

23:16.320 --> 23:17.460
Form 2 or Form X,

23:17.640 --> 23:20.020
they instantly infer its structural meaning.

23:20.380 --> 23:21.960
Even if they've never heard the word before.

23:22.040 --> 23:22.260
Right.

23:22.480 --> 23:23.400
And conversely,

23:23.560 --> 23:25.020
they can take a novel route

23:25.020 --> 23:26.520
and effortlessly generate

23:26.520 --> 23:28.820
the Form X version themselves on the fly.

23:28.900 --> 23:30.180
Which is incredibly efficient.

23:30.460 --> 23:31.000
It is.

23:31.280 --> 23:33.080
But the embodied constraint model

23:33.080 --> 23:34.120
viewed this purely

23:34.120 --> 23:36.120
as an endpoint of cost efficiency.

23:36.580 --> 23:37.720
High distinctness,

23:37.960 --> 23:39.580
low cognitive cost.

23:39.580 --> 23:41.180
Just a really good score

23:41.180 --> 23:41.820
on the ledger bill.

23:41.840 --> 23:42.300
Exactly.

23:42.840 --> 23:43.940
But Flyxion says

23:43.940 --> 23:46.080
they missed the actual mechanism

23:46.080 --> 23:47.220
that makes that efficiency

23:47.220 --> 23:48.500
physically possible.

23:48.500 --> 23:50.280
Predictive generativity

23:50.280 --> 23:51.320
is only possible

23:51.320 --> 23:52.960
because template application

23:52.960 --> 23:54.480
is strictly segregated

23:54.480 --> 23:55.940
to depth zero.

23:56.160 --> 23:56.340
Wait.

23:56.700 --> 23:57.960
Explain that segregation.

23:58.280 --> 23:59.640
If the formation of templates

23:59.640 --> 24:01.820
were a live, fluid option,

24:02.200 --> 24:03.260
if speakers were allowed

24:03.260 --> 24:04.540
to constantly invent

24:04.540 --> 24:05.780
new grammatical structures

24:05.780 --> 24:07.340
on the fly at depth one,

24:07.840 --> 24:09.900
generalization would instantly collapse.

24:10.060 --> 24:10.320
Oh.

24:10.860 --> 24:12.040
Because the baking mold

24:12.040 --> 24:13.680
would constantly be shifting its shape

24:13.680 --> 24:14.240
while you were trying

24:14.240 --> 24:15.040
to stamp the cookie.

24:15.360 --> 24:15.680
Yes.

24:15.800 --> 24:16.360
You wouldn't know

24:16.360 --> 24:17.340
if you were getting a star,

24:17.500 --> 24:18.600
a circle, or a square.

24:18.760 --> 24:20.220
You'd have to relearn the rules

24:20.220 --> 24:21.300
every time someone spoke.

24:21.700 --> 24:22.140
Exactly.

24:23.000 --> 24:23.960
The immense productivity

24:23.960 --> 24:26.160
of Arabic derivational morphology

24:26.160 --> 24:27.840
is a direct consequence

24:27.840 --> 24:29.400
of keeping template formation

24:29.400 --> 24:30.400
historically settled

24:30.400 --> 24:31.180
at depth one,

24:31.700 --> 24:33.260
making it extraordinarily rare

24:33.260 --> 24:33.960
to change,

24:34.180 --> 24:35.760
while keeping template application

24:35.760 --> 24:36.820
at depth zero,

24:37.180 --> 24:39.380
making it infinitely generalizable.

24:39.800 --> 24:40.740
That is brilliant.

24:40.740 --> 24:41.800
If a linguist today

24:41.800 --> 24:43.160
tried to formally propose

24:43.160 --> 24:44.740
an eleventh productive measure,

24:45.200 --> 24:46.440
it would not just be a request

24:46.440 --> 24:47.240
to add a new word

24:47.240 --> 24:47.740
to the dictionary,

24:47.960 --> 24:49.500
it would be a depth one assault

24:49.500 --> 24:50.620
on the generative boundaries

24:50.620 --> 24:51.760
of the language itself.

24:52.000 --> 24:52.320
Wow.

24:53.080 --> 24:55.260
This framework clarifies so much.

24:55.380 --> 24:56.860
It really separates the tools

24:56.860 --> 24:57.520
from the factory

24:57.520 --> 24:58.400
that makes the tools.

24:58.480 --> 24:59.080
It does.

24:59.280 --> 25:00.540
But as we move further

25:00.540 --> 25:01.160
into the paper,

25:01.760 --> 25:03.260
Flyxion raises a complication

25:03.260 --> 25:04.200
that kind of forces us

25:04.200 --> 25:05.140
to test the boundaries

25:05.140 --> 25:05.920
of this whole theory.

25:06.380 --> 25:07.200
We've established

25:07.200 --> 25:08.620
how surface marks operate

25:08.620 --> 25:09.420
at depth zero

25:09.420 --> 25:10.940
and how deep rules

25:10.940 --> 25:12.520
get locked in at depth one.

25:12.960 --> 25:15.040
But can a depth zero surface mark

25:15.040 --> 25:16.680
like a tiny dot or a line

25:16.680 --> 25:18.040
evolve to take on

25:18.040 --> 25:19.480
a massive complex function

25:19.480 --> 25:20.720
without ever actually

25:20.720 --> 25:21.840
moving up to depth one?

25:21.940 --> 25:23.000
That is the big question.

25:23.220 --> 25:23.860
Does the function

25:23.860 --> 25:25.160
of a mark dictate its depth?

25:25.500 --> 25:25.720
Right.

25:25.980 --> 25:27.660
And the paper definitively argues

25:27.660 --> 25:28.920
that function, scope,

25:29.220 --> 25:29.880
and depth

25:29.880 --> 25:31.920
are entirely independent axes.

25:32.120 --> 25:32.940
They aren't tied together.

25:33.580 --> 25:34.420
And to prove this,

25:34.780 --> 25:36.060
Flyxion contrasts

25:36.060 --> 25:37.540
an Arabic orthographic mark

25:37.540 --> 25:39.600
with this fascinating case study

25:39.600 --> 25:40.920
from the evolution of Spanish.

25:41.020 --> 25:42.020
Yes, this is a great section.

25:42.160 --> 25:43.560
Let's begin with the Arabic mark.

25:44.080 --> 25:44.800
The Shadda.

25:44.960 --> 25:46.480
Okay, this is the diacritic mark

25:46.480 --> 25:47.240
used to indicate

25:47.240 --> 25:48.200
consonant doubling

25:48.200 --> 25:48.940
or gemination.

25:49.460 --> 25:50.280
We just talked about this

25:50.280 --> 25:51.840
with Form 2, Fa'ala,

25:52.240 --> 25:54.180
where that middle consonant

25:54.180 --> 25:55.720
is doubled for intensity.

25:56.260 --> 25:57.180
To write that,

25:57.600 --> 25:59.120
you don't draw the letter twice, right?

25:59.120 --> 26:00.600
You just place a small

26:00.600 --> 26:02.360
like or shaped mark

26:02.360 --> 26:03.500
called a Shadda

26:03.500 --> 26:04.680
above the single letter.

26:04.880 --> 26:05.160
Correct.

26:05.600 --> 26:06.560
Under the admissibility

26:06.560 --> 26:07.620
dynamics framework,

26:08.040 --> 26:09.040
the Shadda is a pure

26:09.040 --> 26:10.300
depth zero write.

26:10.540 --> 26:10.800
Okay.

26:10.880 --> 26:12.000
It inserts a single

26:12.000 --> 26:12.960
explicit instruction,

26:13.220 --> 26:14.280
duplicate this consonant,

26:14.700 --> 26:15.760
into the reading of the word.

26:16.020 --> 26:17.020
It does not alter

26:17.020 --> 26:17.940
the generative rules

26:17.940 --> 26:18.520
of the alphabet.

26:19.060 --> 26:19.660
It is simply

26:19.660 --> 26:21.380
an identity duplication operator.

26:21.520 --> 26:21.840
Got it.

26:22.040 --> 26:23.460
It's an incredibly cheap way

26:23.460 --> 26:24.720
in terms of physical effort

26:24.720 --> 26:26.640
to represent a sound change.

26:26.740 --> 26:27.480
You don't have to invent

26:27.480 --> 26:28.040
a new letter.

26:28.140 --> 26:29.360
You just drop a symbol on it.

26:29.700 --> 26:30.140
Exactly.

26:30.480 --> 26:31.160
Now let's examine

26:31.160 --> 26:32.100
a comparative case

26:32.100 --> 26:32.980
to see how the function

26:32.980 --> 26:34.260
of a depth zero mark

26:34.260 --> 26:35.440
can completely transform

26:35.440 --> 26:36.380
across centuries

26:36.380 --> 26:37.840
without ever leaving

26:37.840 --> 26:38.540
depth zero.

26:38.820 --> 26:39.880
We look at the Spanish

26:39.880 --> 26:40.680
any, the nyin.

26:40.920 --> 26:41.480
I have to say,

26:41.660 --> 26:42.480
this is one of my absolute

26:42.480 --> 26:43.800
favorite historical tangents

26:43.800 --> 26:44.660
in the entire paper.

26:45.540 --> 26:46.640
The Spanish nyin

26:46.640 --> 26:47.700
descends from the Latin

26:47.700 --> 26:48.860
double N, right?

26:49.240 --> 26:50.540
The text uses the example

26:50.540 --> 26:51.720
of the Latin word anu,

26:52.080 --> 26:52.900
A-N-N-U,

26:53.120 --> 26:53.660
meaning year.

26:54.260 --> 26:54.660
Today,

26:54.900 --> 26:55.740
that word in Spanish

26:55.740 --> 26:56.620
is año.

26:56.940 --> 26:57.220
Yes.

26:57.540 --> 26:58.660
In the medieval period,

26:58.880 --> 27:00.060
scribes writing in Latin

27:00.060 --> 27:01.420
and early Romance languages

27:01.420 --> 27:03.160
faced a severe economic

27:03.160 --> 27:03.680
constraint,

27:04.020 --> 27:05.000
the cost of parchment.

27:05.300 --> 27:06.400
Back to the animal skins.

27:06.780 --> 27:07.180
Exactly.

27:07.600 --> 27:09.120
They actively sought ways

27:09.120 --> 27:10.260
to compress the physical

27:10.260 --> 27:11.220
footprint of words

27:11.220 --> 27:12.260
to save space.

27:12.600 --> 27:13.580
This is exactly

27:13.580 --> 27:14.600
the kind of flat

27:14.600 --> 27:15.540
economic pressure

27:15.540 --> 27:16.660
the embodied constraint

27:16.660 --> 27:17.460
model highlights.

27:17.960 --> 27:19.000
So to save space,

27:19.220 --> 27:19.800
instead of writing

27:19.800 --> 27:21.100
two Ns sequentially,

27:21.440 --> 27:22.260
scribes began writing

27:22.260 --> 27:23.060
a single N

27:23.060 --> 27:24.180
and placing a small

27:24.180 --> 27:25.740
superscript wave over it

27:25.740 --> 27:26.720
to indicate the missing

27:26.720 --> 27:27.400
second letter.

27:27.660 --> 27:28.860
That is wild.

27:28.860 --> 27:30.060
The tilde was literally

27:30.060 --> 27:31.900
born as a tiny lazy Anne

27:31.900 --> 27:32.760
floating on top

27:32.760 --> 27:33.460
of the main letter,

27:33.920 --> 27:34.600
purely to save

27:34.600 --> 27:35.580
an inch of animal skin.

27:35.800 --> 27:36.700
That's all it was.

27:37.260 --> 27:38.120
At that specific

27:38.120 --> 27:39.220
historical moment,

27:39.440 --> 27:40.240
the tilde was a

27:40.240 --> 27:42.000
depth zero shorthand.

27:42.300 --> 27:43.480
It carried absolutely

27:43.480 --> 27:44.740
no unique phonemic

27:44.740 --> 27:45.300
information.

27:45.840 --> 27:46.520
It was merely

27:46.520 --> 27:47.700
a space-saving

27:47.700 --> 27:48.960
abbreviation for an

27:48.960 --> 27:49.700
already present

27:49.700 --> 27:50.440
double consonant.

27:50.740 --> 27:50.980
Okay.

27:51.200 --> 27:51.900
But then,

27:52.360 --> 27:53.320
the spoken language

27:53.320 --> 27:54.360
began to drift.

27:54.720 --> 27:56.000
The phonetics shifted.

27:56.060 --> 27:57.180
As language always does.

27:57.180 --> 27:58.100
The way people

27:58.100 --> 27:58.840
actually talked

27:58.840 --> 28:00.020
in the streets changed.

28:00.200 --> 28:00.680
Exactly.

28:01.540 --> 28:03.060
The spoken double nasal sound

28:03.060 --> 28:04.040
underwent a process

28:04.040 --> 28:05.220
called palatalization.

28:05.940 --> 28:07.000
It evolved from

28:07.000 --> 28:08.380
a drawn-out and sound

28:08.380 --> 28:09.380
into an entirely

28:09.380 --> 28:10.520
distinct phonome,

28:10.960 --> 28:11.980
the palatal nasal

28:11.980 --> 28:13.300
we hear in Anyu today.

28:13.480 --> 28:14.300
Okay, so the spoken

28:14.300 --> 28:15.420
reality transformed

28:15.420 --> 28:16.020
completely.

28:16.200 --> 28:17.180
But the graphic mark

28:17.180 --> 28:17.760
on the page,

28:17.860 --> 28:18.320
the tilde,

28:18.480 --> 28:19.740
remained visually identical.

28:20.140 --> 28:20.440
However,

28:20.700 --> 28:21.300
its function

28:21.300 --> 28:22.420
migrated completely.

28:22.540 --> 28:23.140
It upgraded.

28:23.280 --> 28:24.000
It went from being

28:24.000 --> 28:25.460
a simple compression tool

28:25.460 --> 28:26.280
to functioning

28:26.280 --> 28:27.660
exactly like the dot

28:27.660 --> 28:28.700
on the Arabic doll.

28:29.100 --> 28:30.260
It became a categorical

28:30.260 --> 28:31.440
phonemic distinguisher.

28:31.640 --> 28:32.220
Because today,

28:32.380 --> 28:33.240
the tilde is the only

28:33.240 --> 28:33.900
thing separating

28:33.900 --> 28:34.660
the word Anya,

28:34.780 --> 28:35.380
meaning year,

28:35.620 --> 28:36.420
from a hypothetical

28:36.420 --> 28:37.340
word Anno.

28:37.660 --> 28:38.040
It doesn't mean

28:38.040 --> 28:38.960
double letter anymore.

28:39.380 --> 28:40.200
It essentially creates

28:40.200 --> 28:40.880
a brand new letter

28:40.880 --> 28:41.380
in the alphabet.

28:41.820 --> 28:42.940
The critical theoretical

28:42.940 --> 28:44.360
insight here is that

28:44.360 --> 28:45.840
throughout this massive

28:45.840 --> 28:47.000
functional migration,

28:47.580 --> 28:48.640
going from a purely

28:48.640 --> 28:50.400
economic compression tool

28:50.400 --> 28:51.460
to a fundamental

28:51.460 --> 28:53.000
phonetic distinguisher,

28:53.620 --> 28:54.420
the mark

28:54.420 --> 28:55.420
never left

28:55.420 --> 28:56.480
depth zero.

28:56.480 --> 28:56.920
Really?

28:57.560 --> 28:58.200
Even though it acts

28:58.200 --> 28:58.800
like a new letter?

28:59.000 --> 28:59.280
Yes.

28:59.920 --> 29:00.680
Both the medieval

29:00.680 --> 29:02.060
abbreviation and the

29:02.060 --> 29:03.040
modern phonemic marker

29:03.040 --> 29:04.080
act as simple

29:04.080 --> 29:05.620
writes into the existing

29:05.620 --> 29:06.940
orthographic inventory.

29:07.820 --> 29:08.580
Neither stage

29:08.580 --> 29:09.580
required rewriting

29:09.580 --> 29:10.220
the fundamental

29:10.220 --> 29:11.160
generative rules

29:11.160 --> 29:11.900
of how the Latin

29:11.900 --> 29:12.940
alphabet connects

29:12.940 --> 29:14.020
or constructs words.

29:14.200 --> 29:14.500
Wow.

29:14.840 --> 29:15.600
The function changed

29:15.600 --> 29:16.080
completely,

29:16.300 --> 29:16.880
but the depth

29:16.880 --> 29:17.760
remained constant.

29:18.220 --> 29:19.160
This definitively

29:19.160 --> 29:20.100
separates the axis

29:20.100 --> 29:21.040
of depth from the

29:21.040 --> 29:21.960
axis of function.

29:22.120 --> 29:22.880
Okay, that makes

29:22.880 --> 29:23.520
so much sense.

29:23.640 --> 29:23.720
Yeah.

29:23.920 --> 29:24.580
So function and depth

29:24.580 --> 29:25.480
are totally independent.

29:25.480 --> 29:26.400
You can change

29:26.400 --> 29:27.200
what a tool does

29:27.200 --> 29:27.880
without changing

29:27.880 --> 29:28.340
what level

29:28.340 --> 29:28.980
it operates on.

29:29.300 --> 29:29.940
But what about scope?

29:30.120 --> 29:31.060
Scope is the next

29:31.060 --> 29:31.800
big variable.

29:31.920 --> 29:32.040
Right.

29:32.100 --> 29:32.900
Does the sheer size

29:32.900 --> 29:33.260
of the thing

29:33.260 --> 29:33.880
being modified

29:33.880 --> 29:34.800
change its depth?

29:35.080 --> 29:35.840
Like if a mark

29:35.840 --> 29:36.820
affects a single letter,

29:37.160 --> 29:38.220
it's depth zero.

29:38.620 --> 29:39.380
But what if it affects

29:39.380 --> 29:40.460
an entire sentence?

29:40.760 --> 29:41.460
Does it graduate

29:41.460 --> 29:42.340
to depth one?

29:43.460 --> 29:44.080
This brings us

29:44.080 --> 29:44.540
to the sukun.

29:44.900 --> 29:45.940
The sukun is a

29:45.940 --> 29:46.920
brilliant operator

29:46.920 --> 29:47.860
to study for this.

29:48.460 --> 29:49.120
Unlike a dot

29:49.120 --> 29:49.700
or a shada,

29:50.040 --> 29:51.060
which add a positive

29:51.060 --> 29:52.060
form or duplicate

29:52.060 --> 29:52.580
a sound,

29:52.720 --> 29:53.500
the sukun marks

29:53.500 --> 29:53.980
an absence.

29:54.340 --> 29:55.140
An absence of what?

29:55.440 --> 29:56.660
It explicitly denotes

29:56.660 --> 29:57.700
the absence of a vowel

29:57.700 --> 29:58.760
following a consonant.

29:59.200 --> 30:00.220
It is a null state.

30:00.820 --> 30:02.100
Flyxion categorizes it

30:02.100 --> 30:03.800
as a constitutive operation

30:03.800 --> 30:05.200
or a boundary marker.

30:05.340 --> 30:05.880
So it's essentially

30:05.880 --> 30:06.460
a stop sign.

30:06.560 --> 30:07.180
It tells the reader,

30:07.600 --> 30:09.040
do not make a vowel sound here.

30:09.140 --> 30:09.760
Stop the airflow.

30:09.960 --> 30:10.380
Exactly.

30:10.680 --> 30:12.100
And Flyxion demonstrates

30:12.100 --> 30:13.700
how this exact same

30:13.700 --> 30:15.700
depth zero stop sign

30:15.700 --> 30:16.840
is deployed at three

30:16.840 --> 30:18.640
exponentially expanding scopes

30:18.640 --> 30:20.020
without ever changing

30:20.020 --> 30:20.780
its fundamental

30:20.780 --> 30:22.020
algorithmic nature.

30:22.020 --> 30:23.020
Okay, let's walk

30:23.020 --> 30:23.560
through these scopes.

30:23.700 --> 30:24.220
Scope one.

30:24.540 --> 30:25.780
Let's examine scope one.

30:26.060 --> 30:26.540
The syllable.

30:26.900 --> 30:28.500
This is the most basic use.

30:28.660 --> 30:30.060
A word internal sukun.

30:30.760 --> 30:31.740
You are reading a word.

30:31.980 --> 30:32.780
You expect a vowel

30:32.780 --> 30:33.780
to follow a consonant,

30:34.100 --> 30:35.420
but the sukun appears.

30:35.880 --> 30:37.000
It closes the syllable

30:37.000 --> 30:37.600
mid-word.

30:38.140 --> 30:38.820
Very straightforward.

30:38.920 --> 30:40.100
Just a tiny stop sign

30:40.100 --> 30:40.700
inside the word.

30:40.780 --> 30:41.060
Got it.

30:41.140 --> 30:42.560
Now we expand the scope

30:42.560 --> 30:43.680
to the grammatical level.

30:43.980 --> 30:44.440
Scope two.

30:44.980 --> 30:46.080
The mood of the verb.

30:46.560 --> 30:47.000
Specifically,

30:47.380 --> 30:48.200
the juicive mood

30:48.200 --> 30:48.900
or majum.

30:49.260 --> 30:50.260
Okay, break that down for me.

30:50.260 --> 30:51.060
In Arabic,

30:51.380 --> 30:52.260
the imperfect herb

30:52.260 --> 30:53.420
has different moods,

30:53.540 --> 30:54.480
much like other languages,

30:54.800 --> 30:55.620
but they are distinguished

30:55.620 --> 30:57.560
solely by the final short vowel.

30:58.400 --> 30:59.420
The indicative mood,

30:59.740 --> 31:00.800
expressing a standard

31:00.800 --> 31:01.640
factual action,

31:02.020 --> 31:02.920
ends with the dhamma,

31:03.580 --> 31:04.440
a wu sound.

31:04.880 --> 31:05.100
So,

31:05.620 --> 31:06.020
yafalu.

31:06.280 --> 31:06.740
Yafalu.

31:06.940 --> 31:08.140
The subjective mood,

31:08.360 --> 31:09.080
used for intent

31:09.080 --> 31:09.820
or possibility,

31:10.160 --> 31:11.100
ends with a fatha,

31:11.380 --> 31:12.120
an a sound.

31:12.540 --> 31:12.840
Yafala.

31:13.020 --> 31:13.380
Got it.

31:13.400 --> 31:13.920
And what happens

31:13.920 --> 31:14.980
when we need the jist of mood,

31:15.080 --> 31:16.160
which is used for commands

31:16.160 --> 31:17.340
or conditional statements?

31:17.340 --> 31:18.620
The juicive mood,

31:18.820 --> 31:19.300
yafala,

31:19.540 --> 31:21.560
carries no final vowel whatsoever.

31:21.700 --> 31:21.860
Oh.

31:22.320 --> 31:23.040
To form it,

31:23.240 --> 31:24.100
the system applies

31:24.100 --> 31:25.240
the exact same

31:25.240 --> 31:26.360
depth zero operator.

31:27.160 --> 31:28.120
A sukun is placed

31:28.120 --> 31:29.040
on the final consonant,

31:29.320 --> 31:30.240
and the brilliance here

31:30.240 --> 31:31.880
is found in the terminology itself.

31:32.260 --> 31:32.920
How so?

31:33.140 --> 31:34.180
The grammatical term

31:34.180 --> 31:35.160
for the juicive mood,

31:35.340 --> 31:35.820
majum,

31:36.020 --> 31:36.920
is derived from

31:36.920 --> 31:38.400
the exact same lexical root

31:38.400 --> 31:39.160
as jasm,

31:39.380 --> 31:40.460
which is the phonetic rule

31:40.460 --> 31:41.280
dictating the use

31:41.280 --> 31:41.960
of the sukun.

31:42.060 --> 31:42.240
Wait,

31:42.300 --> 31:42.860
so the language

31:42.860 --> 31:44.240
takes the exact same

31:44.240 --> 31:45.740
depth zero stop sign

31:45.740 --> 31:47.600
that closes a tiny syllable

31:47.600 --> 31:48.480
inside a word

31:48.480 --> 31:49.680
and reuses it

31:49.680 --> 31:51.160
one grammatical level up

31:51.160 --> 31:52.820
to signal an entirely different

31:52.820 --> 31:54.480
massive structural category

31:54.480 --> 31:55.560
for the verb itself.

31:55.560 --> 31:58.160
It reuses the exact same tool

31:58.160 --> 31:59.540
for a much larger job,

31:59.740 --> 32:01.980
and then the system zooms out

32:01.980 --> 32:03.760
to the largest possible scope.

32:04.420 --> 32:05.040
Scope three,

32:05.840 --> 32:06.560
the utterance,

32:07.080 --> 32:07.860
or wach.

32:08.160 --> 32:08.580
Wash.

32:08.940 --> 32:10.300
This occurs when a reader

32:10.300 --> 32:11.420
reaches the end of a phrase

32:11.420 --> 32:13.760
or needs to pause for breath

32:13.760 --> 32:14.860
during a recitation, right?

32:14.900 --> 32:15.260
Yes.

32:15.600 --> 32:17.120
In continuous Arabic reading,

32:17.380 --> 32:18.940
nouns carry specific endings

32:18.940 --> 32:20.920
denoting case and definiteness.

32:21.300 --> 32:22.280
An indefinite noun

32:22.280 --> 32:23.300
in the nominative case

32:23.300 --> 32:23.980
carries a marker

32:23.980 --> 32:24.760
called tanwin,

32:25.120 --> 32:26.400
which is pronounced as un.

32:26.640 --> 32:27.420
Take the word

32:27.420 --> 32:28.320
for the letter alif.

32:28.680 --> 32:29.940
If it is indefinite

32:29.940 --> 32:30.500
and continuous,

32:30.780 --> 32:31.920
it is pronounced elephant.

32:32.520 --> 32:33.540
This unending

32:33.540 --> 32:34.600
performs the same

32:34.600 --> 32:35.700
morphological function

32:35.700 --> 32:36.780
that the English article

32:36.780 --> 32:38.480
A performs syntactically.

32:38.960 --> 32:39.460
An alif.

32:39.700 --> 32:40.340
But when the reader

32:40.340 --> 32:41.340
reaches a full stop,

32:41.560 --> 32:42.520
like the end of a sentence.

32:42.820 --> 32:43.500
At a pause,

32:43.620 --> 32:45.220
this ending is entirely dropped.

32:45.620 --> 32:46.940
Alif instantly becomes

32:46.940 --> 32:47.740
simply alif.

32:48.060 --> 32:48.920
The final vowel

32:48.920 --> 32:49.680
and the nanation

32:49.680 --> 32:50.340
just vanish.

32:50.820 --> 32:52.120
The formal grammatical rule

32:52.120 --> 32:53.020
governing this pause

32:53.020 --> 32:54.240
dictates that the last letter

32:54.240 --> 32:55.380
must be made soken,

32:55.640 --> 32:57.180
deploying the same root word

32:57.180 --> 32:57.700
yet again.

32:57.720 --> 32:58.840
As the exact same

32:58.840 --> 32:59.680
closure operator.

33:00.000 --> 33:01.120
It is applied to the boundary

33:01.120 --> 33:02.300
of an entire phrase

33:02.300 --> 33:03.020
or utterance.

33:03.580 --> 33:04.780
A reader utilizes

33:04.780 --> 33:06.060
this dropping of sound

33:06.060 --> 33:07.560
in the exact same manner

33:07.560 --> 33:08.540
we use a period

33:08.540 --> 33:09.480
in written English.

33:09.680 --> 33:09.960
Right.

33:09.960 --> 33:11.160
The sudden disappearance

33:11.160 --> 33:12.560
of an expected sound

33:12.560 --> 33:13.860
is itself

33:13.860 --> 33:15.240
the positive signal

33:15.240 --> 33:16.500
that a massive cognitive

33:16.500 --> 33:17.360
unit of thought

33:17.360 --> 33:18.080
has concluded.

33:18.560 --> 33:19.700
I want to make sure

33:19.700 --> 33:21.060
I am fully grasping

33:21.060 --> 33:22.000
the sheer scale

33:22.000 --> 33:22.820
of this reuse

33:22.820 --> 33:24.080
because it's so cool.

33:24.540 --> 33:25.020
Let's stick with

33:25.020 --> 33:26.080
the stop sign visualization.

33:26.360 --> 33:26.760
Go for it.

33:26.760 --> 33:28.120
Scope 1 is putting

33:28.120 --> 33:29.540
that physical red

33:29.540 --> 33:30.260
stop sign

33:30.260 --> 33:31.260
at the end

33:31.260 --> 33:31.840
of a single

33:31.840 --> 33:32.780
residential block.

33:33.040 --> 33:34.020
Just stopping a syllable.

33:34.600 --> 33:35.560
Scope 2 is taking

33:35.560 --> 33:36.600
that exact same

33:36.600 --> 33:37.200
stop sign

33:37.200 --> 33:38.080
and placing it

33:38.080 --> 33:38.640
at the boundary

33:38.640 --> 33:39.660
of a whole neighborhood

33:39.660 --> 33:40.960
to denote a completely

33:40.960 --> 33:42.120
different zoning law.

33:42.500 --> 33:43.440
Stopping the mood

33:43.440 --> 33:44.080
of the verb.

33:44.220 --> 33:44.640
Yes.

33:44.960 --> 33:46.180
And scope 3 is taking

33:46.180 --> 33:47.460
that identical stop sign

33:47.460 --> 33:48.300
and planting it

33:48.300 --> 33:48.820
on the highway

33:48.820 --> 33:49.480
at the city limit

33:49.480 --> 33:50.840
to say the entire city

33:50.840 --> 33:51.440
ends here.

33:51.740 --> 33:52.660
Stopping the whole utterance.

33:52.960 --> 33:54.160
But through all of this

33:54.160 --> 33:55.320
the physical find itself

33:55.320 --> 33:55.900
hasn't changed

33:55.900 --> 33:56.860
its fundamental nature

33:56.860 --> 33:57.260
at all.

33:57.680 --> 33:58.420
It is still just

33:58.420 --> 33:59.240
a piece of metal

33:59.240 --> 33:59.940
painted red.

34:00.100 --> 34:01.800
That is a perfect visualization.

34:02.400 --> 34:02.980
Three scopes

34:02.980 --> 34:04.060
one operator.

34:04.680 --> 34:05.280
A syllable

34:05.280 --> 34:06.680
a grammatical mood

34:06.680 --> 34:07.900
a complete utterance

34:07.900 --> 34:10.020
and in every single instance

34:10.020 --> 34:11.740
the operation remains

34:11.740 --> 34:13.320
a depth zero right.

34:13.760 --> 34:14.780
It's just wild.

34:14.940 --> 34:15.980
It never rewrites

34:15.980 --> 34:17.040
the generative rules

34:17.040 --> 34:17.700
of the language.

34:18.080 --> 34:19.480
It simply executes

34:19.480 --> 34:20.060
a command

34:20.060 --> 34:21.060
against the background

34:21.060 --> 34:21.580
assumption

34:21.580 --> 34:23.320
that vowels continue

34:23.320 --> 34:24.800
unless explicitly

34:24.800 --> 34:25.600
marked otherwise.

34:26.160 --> 34:27.000
This just proves

34:27.000 --> 34:27.780
without a doubt

34:27.780 --> 34:29.120
that depth and scope

34:29.120 --> 34:30.520
are fundamentally decoupled.

34:31.260 --> 34:31.740
An operation

34:31.740 --> 34:32.300
can remain

34:32.300 --> 34:32.840
a microscopic

34:32.840 --> 34:34.280
depth zero tweak

34:34.280 --> 34:35.640
even while the size

34:35.640 --> 34:36.640
of the linguistic unit

34:36.640 --> 34:37.120
it controls

34:37.120 --> 34:38.100
grows exponentially.

34:38.360 --> 34:39.300
Completely independent.

34:39.740 --> 34:40.900
But this naturally

34:40.900 --> 34:42.000
forces us to confront

34:42.000 --> 34:44.900
a very chaotic reality

34:44.900 --> 34:45.760
because if we have

34:45.760 --> 34:46.680
independent functions

34:46.680 --> 34:48.020
and independent scopes

34:48.020 --> 34:49.100
what happens

34:49.100 --> 34:49.960
inside a language

34:49.960 --> 34:51.100
when two completely

34:51.100 --> 34:52.580
independent depth one rules

34:52.580 --> 34:53.780
crash into each other

34:53.780 --> 34:54.840
within a single word.

34:55.120 --> 34:55.740
I mean language

34:55.740 --> 34:56.680
isn't a clean

34:56.680 --> 34:57.780
isolated laboratory.

34:58.100 --> 34:58.660
Things collide

34:58.660 --> 34:59.260
all the time.

34:59.340 --> 35:00.280
They absolutely do

35:00.280 --> 35:00.920
and Flyxion

35:00.920 --> 35:01.560
addresses this

35:01.560 --> 35:02.200
by analyzing

35:02.200 --> 35:03.260
how rules compose

35:03.260 --> 35:03.880
and interact

35:03.880 --> 35:04.860
with the boundary cases.

35:05.320 --> 35:05.780
Let's look at how

35:05.780 --> 35:06.380
verbs stems

35:06.380 --> 35:07.320
and pronouns interact.

35:07.440 --> 35:08.040
Okay let's look

35:08.040 --> 35:08.580
at the collision.

35:08.860 --> 35:09.560
We established

35:09.560 --> 35:10.260
that generating

35:10.260 --> 35:10.860
a verb stem

35:10.860 --> 35:11.840
selecting the template

35:11.840 --> 35:12.700
which we will call

35:12.700 --> 35:12.940
T

35:12.940 --> 35:14.440
is a depth one rule.

35:14.860 --> 35:15.700
It is a historically

35:15.700 --> 35:16.780
locked in piece

35:16.780 --> 35:17.400
of machinery.

35:17.920 --> 35:19.100
But a stem alone

35:19.100 --> 35:20.400
is not a usable verb

35:20.400 --> 35:21.120
in a sentence.

35:21.540 --> 35:22.520
You must conjugate it

35:22.520 --> 35:23.380
for person,

35:23.620 --> 35:23.920
gender,

35:24.100 --> 35:24.640
and number.

35:24.860 --> 35:25.260
Right you have to

35:25.260 --> 35:25.960
specify if it's

35:25.960 --> 35:26.600
I do,

35:26.820 --> 35:27.360
she does,

35:27.420 --> 35:28.360
or they do.

35:28.580 --> 35:29.960
The paper lists out

35:29.960 --> 35:30.820
the affixes used

35:30.820 --> 35:31.180
for this

35:31.180 --> 35:31.780
which we can call

35:31.780 --> 35:31.980
P.

35:32.320 --> 35:32.640
Yes.

35:32.860 --> 35:33.560
So if we take

35:33.560 --> 35:34.320
our base stem

35:34.320 --> 35:34.800
faala

35:34.800 --> 35:35.900
and I want to say

35:35.900 --> 35:36.260
I do

35:36.260 --> 35:37.540
I add a prefix

35:37.540 --> 35:38.060
and it becomes

35:38.060 --> 35:39.060
a falu.

35:39.060 --> 35:39.720
I want to say

35:39.720 --> 35:40.360
they do

35:40.360 --> 35:41.700
like masculine plural

35:41.700 --> 35:42.420
it becomes

35:42.420 --> 35:43.000
ya faluna.

35:43.360 --> 35:44.020
These prefixes

35:44.020 --> 35:44.760
and suffixes

35:44.760 --> 35:45.180
P

35:45.180 --> 35:46.640
belong to an entirely

35:46.640 --> 35:47.700
separate depth one

35:47.700 --> 35:48.460
rule paradigm.

35:48.740 --> 35:49.340
They are their own

35:49.340 --> 35:50.240
enclosed system.

35:50.680 --> 35:51.460
And the crucial

35:51.460 --> 35:52.000
observation

35:52.000 --> 35:52.740
Felixson makes

35:52.740 --> 35:53.360
is that neither

35:53.360 --> 35:54.540
paradigm modifies

35:54.540 --> 35:55.060
the other.

35:55.260 --> 35:55.760
They don't mess

35:55.760 --> 35:56.540
with each other's rules.

35:56.740 --> 35:57.220
Not at all.

35:57.400 --> 35:58.240
Selecting a measure

35:58.240 --> 35:59.300
T and selecting

35:59.300 --> 36:00.040
an affix P

36:00.040 --> 36:00.840
are strictly

36:00.840 --> 36:02.160
independent operations.

36:02.820 --> 36:04.080
The final spoken word

36:04.080 --> 36:04.760
is a pure

36:04.760 --> 36:05.900
mathematical composition.

36:06.440 --> 36:07.440
The word equals P

36:07.440 --> 36:08.200
applied to T

36:08.200 --> 36:09.140
applied to the root.

36:09.400 --> 36:10.220
So because both

36:10.220 --> 36:11.060
of these massive

36:11.060 --> 36:12.160
architectural rules

36:12.160 --> 36:13.140
are safely locked

36:13.140 --> 36:14.120
away at depth one

36:14.120 --> 36:15.580
a speaker doesn't

36:15.580 --> 36:16.340
have to constantly

36:16.340 --> 36:17.340
renegotiate them

36:17.340 --> 36:17.960
when they talk.

36:17.960 --> 36:18.960
The speaker can

36:18.960 --> 36:19.620
just take them

36:19.620 --> 36:21.280
and rapidly compose

36:21.280 --> 36:22.500
infinite novel forms

36:22.500 --> 36:23.240
on the fly

36:23.240 --> 36:23.980
at depth zero.

36:24.480 --> 36:25.320
The rules don't

36:25.320 --> 36:26.020
interfere with each

36:26.020 --> 36:26.160
other.

36:26.240 --> 36:26.940
They just stack.

36:27.400 --> 36:27.840
Exactly.

36:28.020 --> 36:28.540
They stack

36:28.540 --> 36:29.220
predictably.

36:29.680 --> 36:30.580
And we see this

36:30.580 --> 36:31.220
principle of

36:31.220 --> 36:32.020
independent rules

36:32.020 --> 36:33.080
operating in parallel

36:33.080 --> 36:34.080
everywhere in the

36:34.080 --> 36:34.340
script.

36:35.100 --> 36:35.720
Consider the

36:35.720 --> 36:36.120
Hamza,

36:36.300 --> 36:37.260
the glottal stop.

36:37.400 --> 36:37.680
Oh yeah,

36:37.760 --> 36:38.320
the paper goes

36:38.320 --> 36:39.240
into detail on this.

36:39.360 --> 36:39.960
The rule for

36:39.960 --> 36:41.160
choosing which seat

36:41.160 --> 36:42.200
the Hamza sits on

36:42.200 --> 36:43.220
whether it rests on

36:43.220 --> 36:43.740
an alif,

36:43.920 --> 36:44.260
a wa,

36:44.480 --> 36:44.900
a yo,

36:44.900 --> 36:45.960
or simply floats

36:45.960 --> 36:46.860
independently on the

36:46.860 --> 36:48.420
line is governed by

36:48.420 --> 36:49.400
a very strict

36:49.400 --> 36:50.380
vowel strength

36:50.380 --> 36:50.900
hierarchy.

36:51.420 --> 36:51.980
I remember this.

36:52.060 --> 36:52.880
The paper outlines

36:52.880 --> 36:53.820
the hierarchy right.

36:54.060 --> 36:54.480
The kasra,

36:54.560 --> 36:55.240
the I sound,

36:55.340 --> 36:55.980
is the strongest.

36:56.440 --> 36:56.960
Then the dham,

36:57.040 --> 36:57.620
the you sound.

36:57.860 --> 36:58.300
Then the fada,

36:58.400 --> 36:58.900
the I sound.

36:59.360 --> 37:00.120
And the sukun,

37:00.200 --> 37:00.760
the null state we

37:00.760 --> 37:01.420
just talked about,

37:01.560 --> 37:02.080
is the weakest.

37:02.440 --> 37:02.820
Correct.

37:03.380 --> 37:03.940
The historical

37:03.940 --> 37:05.020
codification of that

37:05.020 --> 37:06.020
specific hierarchy

37:06.020 --> 37:07.000
was a monumental

37:07.000 --> 37:07.900
depth one event.

37:08.220 --> 37:08.900
It set the rules.

37:09.500 --> 37:09.780
Today,

37:09.980 --> 37:10.780
every single time

37:10.780 --> 37:11.640
a writer constructs

37:11.640 --> 37:12.320
a word containing

37:12.320 --> 37:12.780
a Hamza,

37:13.120 --> 37:13.780
they run that

37:13.780 --> 37:14.600
precise algorithm

37:14.600 --> 37:15.220
in their head.

37:15.800 --> 37:16.320
Subconsciously,

37:16.360 --> 37:16.640
probably.

37:16.820 --> 37:17.060
Right.

37:17.300 --> 37:18.020
They evaluate

37:18.020 --> 37:19.160
the vowel of the Hamza,

37:19.320 --> 37:19.800
they evaluate

37:19.800 --> 37:20.420
the vowel of the

37:20.420 --> 37:21.040
preceding letter,

37:21.280 --> 37:21.760
they compare

37:21.760 --> 37:22.320
their relative

37:22.320 --> 37:23.140
strengths according

37:23.140 --> 37:23.880
to the hierarchy,

37:24.200 --> 37:25.120
and they assign

37:25.120 --> 37:25.940
the seat based

37:25.940 --> 37:26.620
on the victor.

37:27.080 --> 37:28.080
But executing

37:28.080 --> 37:29.040
that algorithmic

37:29.040 --> 37:30.040
check is depth

37:30.040 --> 37:30.480
zero.

37:30.840 --> 37:31.480
It's just running

37:31.480 --> 37:31.960
the program.

37:32.400 --> 37:33.300
And that Hamza

37:33.300 --> 37:34.020
rule operates

37:34.020 --> 37:34.980
in total isolation

37:34.980 --> 37:36.420
from other equally

37:36.420 --> 37:37.460
massive classification

37:37.460 --> 37:38.840
systems in the

37:38.840 --> 37:39.240
language,

37:39.520 --> 37:40.200
like the rules

37:40.200 --> 37:40.940
governing the

37:40.940 --> 37:41.840
noon sakina

37:41.840 --> 37:42.620
and tongue win.

37:42.700 --> 37:42.940
Yes,

37:42.940 --> 37:43.400
that's another

37:43.400 --> 37:44.420
massive taxonomy.

37:44.620 --> 37:45.100
I want to break

37:45.100 --> 37:45.660
this one down

37:45.660 --> 37:46.360
because it shows

37:46.360 --> 37:46.980
how rigid

37:46.980 --> 37:47.900
this stuff can be.

37:48.420 --> 37:49.540
When a noon sound,

37:49.780 --> 37:50.600
an N sound,

37:50.680 --> 37:51.380
meets a consonant,

37:51.860 --> 37:52.680
the pronunciation

37:52.680 --> 37:53.940
shifts based on

37:53.940 --> 37:54.680
four distinct

37:54.680 --> 37:55.120
treatments.

37:55.620 --> 37:56.220
Let's list them

37:56.220 --> 37:56.800
to see how this

37:56.800 --> 37:57.620
taxonomy actually

37:57.620 --> 37:58.500
works in practice.

37:58.760 --> 37:59.360
It is a perfect

37:59.360 --> 38:00.080
closed system.

38:00.400 --> 38:00.620
First,

38:00.720 --> 38:01.360
there is Eidhar,

38:01.600 --> 38:02.280
which dictates

38:02.280 --> 38:03.060
clear pronunciation.

38:03.560 --> 38:04.300
This occurs when

38:04.300 --> 38:05.080
the noon sound

38:05.080 --> 38:05.780
is followed by

38:05.780 --> 38:06.560
the throat letters.

38:06.760 --> 38:07.000
Okay,

38:07.140 --> 38:07.640
throat letters

38:07.640 --> 38:08.560
get clear pronunciation.

38:08.980 --> 38:09.600
Second is

38:09.600 --> 38:11.260
ism or assimilation.

38:11.780 --> 38:12.560
The noon sound

38:12.560 --> 38:13.380
physically melts

38:13.380 --> 38:14.020
into the following

38:14.020 --> 38:14.520
consonant.

38:15.280 --> 38:15.920
This is triggered

38:15.920 --> 38:16.720
by nasals and

38:16.720 --> 38:17.060
liquids,

38:17.380 --> 38:17.880
such as

38:17.880 --> 38:18.620
lam,

38:19.240 --> 38:19.520
ra,

38:20.180 --> 38:20.540
meme,

38:21.100 --> 38:21.580
and ya.

38:21.720 --> 38:22.280
It just blends

38:22.280 --> 38:22.640
right in.

38:22.780 --> 38:23.500
Third is

38:23.500 --> 38:24.120
iklab,

38:24.500 --> 38:25.360
a fascinating

38:25.360 --> 38:26.360
conversion where

38:26.360 --> 38:27.260
the noon sound

38:27.260 --> 38:28.380
transforms entirely

38:28.380 --> 38:29.360
into a meme,

38:29.760 --> 38:30.580
an M sound.

38:31.060 --> 38:31.900
This is highly

38:31.900 --> 38:33.020
specific and only

38:33.020 --> 38:34.060
occurs before one

38:34.060 --> 38:34.880
single letter,

38:35.680 --> 38:36.100
the ba.

38:36.100 --> 38:37.640
Just before a B?

38:37.780 --> 38:38.640
That's so specific.

38:38.780 --> 38:39.160
It is.

38:39.280 --> 38:39.780
And finally,

38:39.980 --> 38:40.320
ikfa,

38:40.620 --> 38:41.100
which is a

38:41.100 --> 38:42.520
concealed nasalized

38:42.520 --> 38:43.820
pronunciation applied

38:43.820 --> 38:44.800
to all the remaining

38:44.800 --> 38:45.620
consonants in the

38:45.620 --> 38:45.900
alphabet.

38:46.480 --> 38:47.460
So if I am a student

38:47.460 --> 38:48.640
learning to recite this,

38:48.920 --> 38:49.700
I have to mentally

38:49.700 --> 38:51.020
categorize the entire

38:51.020 --> 38:52.060
alphabet into those

38:52.060 --> 38:52.720
four buckets.

38:53.100 --> 38:54.200
It is a massive

38:54.200 --> 38:55.580
depth one taxonomy

38:55.580 --> 38:56.140
to memorize.

38:56.460 --> 38:56.900
It is.

38:57.200 --> 38:58.240
But observe how it

38:58.240 --> 38:58.860
interacts with the

38:58.860 --> 38:59.580
rest of the language.

39:00.180 --> 39:00.820
This four-way

39:00.820 --> 39:01.880
classification exists

39:01.880 --> 39:03.120
alongside an entirely

39:03.120 --> 39:04.340
separate, equally

39:04.340 --> 39:05.380
massive classification

39:05.380 --> 39:06.080
of the alphabet

39:06.080 --> 39:07.420
into sun and moon

39:07.420 --> 39:08.440
letters, which governs

39:08.440 --> 39:09.460
how definite articles

39:09.460 --> 39:10.020
assimilate.

39:10.280 --> 39:10.660
Oh, right.

39:10.720 --> 39:11.380
So they overlap

39:11.380 --> 39:12.160
physically in the

39:12.160 --> 39:12.900
words you're speaking,

39:13.200 --> 39:13.620
but they don't

39:13.620 --> 39:14.460
logically dictate

39:14.460 --> 39:14.940
each other.

39:15.120 --> 39:16.120
They coexist without

39:16.120 --> 39:17.040
cross-interference.

39:17.460 --> 39:18.100
And this provides

39:18.100 --> 39:19.100
vital evidence for

39:19.100 --> 39:19.860
afflictions theory.

39:20.340 --> 39:21.440
Depth one stabilizations

39:21.440 --> 39:22.180
happen locally,

39:22.400 --> 39:23.100
rule by rule,

39:23.320 --> 39:24.460
as isolated historical

39:24.460 --> 39:24.860
events.

39:25.140 --> 39:26.120
They do not happen as

39:26.120 --> 39:26.800
one globally

39:26.800 --> 39:28.160
synchronized, top-down

39:28.160 --> 39:29.200
master plan for the

39:29.200 --> 39:29.540
language.

39:29.900 --> 39:30.620
It's not like someone

39:30.620 --> 39:31.620
sat down and designed

39:31.620 --> 39:32.620
the whole language in a

39:32.620 --> 39:32.900
day.

39:33.100 --> 39:33.760
It's a bunch of

39:33.760 --> 39:35.000
isolated depth one

39:35.000 --> 39:36.180
rules stacking on top

39:36.180 --> 39:36.700
of each other.

39:37.320 --> 39:38.100
Okay, this all sounds

39:38.100 --> 39:38.840
like an incredibly

39:38.840 --> 39:40.120
elegant, perfectly

39:40.120 --> 39:41.900
tuned machine, but

39:41.900 --> 39:43.140
Flyxion admits that

39:43.140 --> 39:43.900
not everything in

39:43.900 --> 39:44.760
human language is

39:44.760 --> 39:45.900
cleanly depth zero

39:45.900 --> 39:47.060
or depth one, right?

39:47.200 --> 39:48.220
No, language is

39:48.220 --> 39:48.880
always messy.

39:49.100 --> 39:49.920
There is a massive

39:49.920 --> 39:51.420
complication in Arabic

39:51.420 --> 39:52.940
morphology that kind

39:52.940 --> 39:54.580
of throws a wrench

39:54.580 --> 39:55.640
into this predictable

39:55.640 --> 39:56.180
machine.

39:56.520 --> 39:58.360
Broken plurals, or

39:58.360 --> 39:59.240
jamtuxir.

39:59.340 --> 40:00.000
Ah, yes.

40:00.540 --> 40:01.200
Broken plurals.

40:01.200 --> 40:02.320
They resist clean

40:02.320 --> 40:03.600
mathematical classification,

40:04.020 --> 40:05.120
and analyzing why they

40:05.120 --> 40:06.320
resist it reveals the

40:06.320 --> 40:07.740
limits of pure generative

40:07.740 --> 40:08.360
systems.

40:08.520 --> 40:09.660
Because, unlike a sound

40:09.660 --> 40:10.560
plural where you just,

40:10.720 --> 40:11.780
you know, slap a suffix

40:11.780 --> 40:12.800
onto the end of a word,

40:13.160 --> 40:14.180
which is a clear, easily

40:14.180 --> 40:15.760
executed depth zero rule,

40:16.280 --> 40:17.460
breaking plurals fundamentally

40:17.460 --> 40:18.940
change the internal vowel

40:18.940 --> 40:20.500
structure of the singular

40:20.500 --> 40:20.920
noun.

40:21.100 --> 40:22.220
It breaks the root open.

40:22.400 --> 40:22.600
Right.

40:23.000 --> 40:24.240
So a book, kitab,

40:24.780 --> 40:25.540
becomes kutab.

40:25.740 --> 40:26.780
A pen, qualum,

40:26.840 --> 40:27.560
becomes a klom.

40:27.780 --> 40:28.740
A man, rajul,

40:28.980 --> 40:29.660
becomes real.

40:29.660 --> 40:30.760
On the surface,

40:30.880 --> 40:31.700
this transformation looks

40:31.700 --> 40:32.760
exactly like the verb

40:32.760 --> 40:33.660
templates we analyzed

40:33.660 --> 40:34.040
earlier.

40:34.220 --> 40:35.320
It appears to be a fixed

40:35.320 --> 40:36.280
set of molds applied

40:36.280 --> 40:37.800
to a root, but it lacks

40:37.800 --> 40:38.780
the core feature of the

40:38.780 --> 40:39.440
verb system.

40:40.040 --> 40:40.560
Predictability.

40:40.800 --> 40:41.280
Exactly.

40:41.820 --> 40:42.340
Predictability.

40:43.120 --> 40:44.240
There are roughly 30

40:44.240 --> 40:45.300
common patterns for

40:45.300 --> 40:46.100
broken plurals.

40:46.880 --> 40:48.300
Crucially, a speaker

40:48.300 --> 40:49.760
cannot reliably predict

40:49.760 --> 40:51.320
which singular noun

40:51.320 --> 40:52.200
will adopt which

40:52.200 --> 40:53.520
specific broken plural

40:53.520 --> 40:55.320
pattern based on any

40:55.320 --> 40:56.580
strict, overarching

40:56.580 --> 40:57.760
phonological rule.

40:57.880 --> 40:58.660
So I can't just

40:58.660 --> 40:59.700
encounter a brand new

40:59.700 --> 41:00.920
noun, run a quick

41:00.920 --> 41:02.020
algorithm in my head,

41:02.100 --> 41:03.360
and confidently generate

41:03.360 --> 41:04.720
the correct broken plural.

41:04.960 --> 41:06.060
No, you cannot.

41:06.600 --> 41:07.540
A substantial number

41:07.540 --> 41:08.540
of them simply have to

41:08.540 --> 41:09.460
be memorized on a

41:09.460 --> 41:10.960
case-by-case lexical

41:10.960 --> 41:11.280
basis.

41:11.320 --> 41:11.420
What?

41:11.780 --> 41:13.060
It instantly reminds me

41:13.060 --> 41:14.320
of how frustrating it is

41:14.320 --> 41:15.740
to learn irregular verbs

41:15.740 --> 41:16.300
in English.

41:16.680 --> 41:17.780
Like, you just have to

41:17.780 --> 41:18.920
know, through sheer

41:18.920 --> 41:19.880
rote memorization,

41:20.340 --> 41:21.440
that the past tense of

41:21.440 --> 41:23.380
run is ran and not

41:23.380 --> 41:23.880
runned.

41:24.320 --> 41:24.980
You don't solve an

41:24.980 --> 41:25.880
equation to find ran.

41:25.880 --> 41:26.780
You have this giant

41:26.780 --> 41:27.980
filing cabinet in your

41:27.980 --> 41:29.080
brain, and you just

41:29.080 --> 41:29.840
have to open the drawer

41:29.840 --> 41:31.300
marked RUN to find the

41:31.300 --> 41:31.600
answer.

41:32.100 --> 41:32.940
That is precisely how

41:32.940 --> 41:34.240
Flyxion categorizes the

41:34.240 --> 41:35.400
cognitive process here.

41:35.820 --> 41:36.760
The paper argues that

41:36.760 --> 41:37.580
retrieving a broken

41:37.580 --> 41:39.100
plural acts less like

41:39.100 --> 41:40.280
executing a generative

41:40.280 --> 41:41.540
mathematical rule and

41:41.540 --> 41:42.140
more like an

41:42.140 --> 41:43.140
interrogative lookup

41:43.140 --> 41:43.860
against a loosely

41:43.860 --> 41:44.740
rule-governed

41:44.740 --> 41:45.480
stored table.

41:45.680 --> 41:46.800
An interrogative lookup.

41:46.840 --> 41:47.420
You're just searching

41:47.420 --> 41:48.220
a database.

41:48.660 --> 41:49.620
It forces the framework

41:49.620 --> 41:50.780
to acknowledge that not

41:50.780 --> 41:51.920
all morphological

41:51.920 --> 41:53.500
stabilization is pure

41:53.500 --> 41:54.780
computed derivation.

41:54.780 --> 41:56.500
A significant portion

41:56.500 --> 41:57.480
of it is stabilized

41:57.480 --> 41:58.900
through brute force

41:58.900 --> 41:59.840
lexical memory.

42:00.180 --> 42:01.040
So it just exists in

42:01.040 --> 42:01.900
this murky middle

42:01.900 --> 42:02.320
ground.

42:02.840 --> 42:03.500
It's not a pure

42:03.500 --> 42:04.880
depth-zero execution

42:04.880 --> 42:05.760
because there is no

42:05.760 --> 42:07.540
determinate single

42:07.540 --> 42:09.040
rule to execute, but

42:09.040 --> 42:10.020
it's not a depth-one

42:10.020 --> 42:11.260
generative rule either

42:11.260 --> 42:12.620
because memorizing

42:12.620 --> 42:13.820
that ki-tub becomes

42:13.820 --> 42:15.080
ku-tub doesn't

42:15.080 --> 42:16.160
fundamentally change

42:16.160 --> 42:17.160
the overall inventory

42:17.160 --> 42:18.080
of the 30 plural

42:18.080 --> 42:18.640
patterns.

42:18.920 --> 42:19.180
Right.

42:19.380 --> 42:20.220
And acknowledging this

42:20.220 --> 42:21.440
messy reality actually

42:21.440 --> 42:22.680
strengthens Flyxion's

42:22.680 --> 42:23.520
overall framework.

42:23.520 --> 42:25.240
By mapping out exactly

42:25.240 --> 42:25.880
where the pure

42:25.880 --> 42:27.240
generative math breaks

42:27.240 --> 42:28.260
down into lexical

42:28.260 --> 42:29.620
memorization, it

42:29.620 --> 42:30.780
highlights exactly how

42:30.780 --> 42:32.160
powerful and rare the

42:32.160 --> 42:33.020
true depth-one

42:33.020 --> 42:34.360
stabilizations actually

42:34.360 --> 42:34.900
are.

42:35.380 --> 42:36.180
Which brings us to the

42:36.180 --> 42:37.060
devastating conclusion

42:37.060 --> 42:37.560
of the paper.

42:37.940 --> 42:38.680
With all of these

42:38.680 --> 42:39.800
nuances laid out, you

42:39.800 --> 42:40.380
know, the independent

42:40.380 --> 42:41.460
scopes, the parallel

42:41.460 --> 42:42.320
rules, the memorized

42:42.320 --> 42:44.060
exceptions, Flyxion brings

42:44.060 --> 42:45.140
the hammer down on that

42:45.140 --> 42:46.880
original flat cost-benefit

42:46.880 --> 42:48.020
formula we started with.

42:48.080 --> 42:49.140
The embodied constraint

42:49.140 --> 42:49.500
model.

42:49.840 --> 42:50.080
Yeah.

42:50.700 --> 42:51.740
We have to look at the

42:51.740 --> 42:53.520
true cost of reversal and

42:53.520 --> 42:55.160
why the math of S equals

42:55.160 --> 42:56.660
alpha-D minus beta-C

42:56.660 --> 42:58.420
completely breaks when

42:58.420 --> 42:59.640
confronted with reality.

43:00.120 --> 43:00.960
Under that flat

43:00.960 --> 43:02.100
mathematical equation,

43:02.360 --> 43:03.540
undoing a change is

43:03.540 --> 43:04.780
assumed to be completely

43:04.780 --> 43:05.940
symmetrical to adopting

43:05.940 --> 43:06.200
it.

43:06.740 --> 43:07.860
It envisions language

43:07.860 --> 43:09.120
evolution as a slider

43:09.120 --> 43:10.540
moving smoothly back and

43:10.540 --> 43:11.400
forth on a track.

43:11.520 --> 43:12.740
Just a sliding scale of

43:12.740 --> 43:13.100
cost.

43:13.300 --> 43:13.540
Right.

43:13.840 --> 43:14.580
If the weighting

43:14.580 --> 43:15.700
parameters shift, for

43:15.700 --> 43:17.300
example, if a society

43:17.300 --> 43:18.440
goes through a dark age

43:18.440 --> 43:19.580
and parchment becomes

43:19.580 --> 43:20.920
astronomically expensive,

43:21.300 --> 43:22.260
heavily weighting the

43:22.260 --> 43:24.020
cost variable, the model

43:24.020 --> 43:24.800
assumes the writing

43:24.800 --> 43:26.160
system will simply slide

43:26.160 --> 43:27.560
backward, systematically

43:27.560 --> 43:29.220
dropping distinctness to

43:29.220 --> 43:29.880
save money.

43:30.080 --> 43:31.440
But Flyxion argues this is

43:31.440 --> 43:33.120
fundamentally false when we

43:33.120 --> 43:33.860
look at depth one

43:33.860 --> 43:34.360
changes.

43:35.120 --> 43:36.360
Reversibility isn't a single

43:36.360 --> 43:36.760
slider.

43:37.080 --> 43:38.320
It depends entirely on

43:38.320 --> 43:38.620
depth.

43:39.060 --> 43:40.380
Let's trace the mechanics of

43:40.380 --> 43:41.640
reversal at both levels.

43:41.800 --> 43:42.020
Okay.

43:42.660 --> 43:44.120
Reversing a depth zero change

43:44.120 --> 43:45.200
is mechanically simple.

43:45.600 --> 43:46.920
If a society decided it

43:46.920 --> 43:48.420
wanted to undot the Arabic

43:48.420 --> 43:49.700
alphabet and return to the

43:49.700 --> 43:51.460
era of skeletal ambiguity,

43:52.100 --> 43:53.120
scribes would simply stop

43:53.120 --> 43:53.860
drawing the dots.

43:54.040 --> 43:54.960
You just don't pick up the

43:54.960 --> 43:55.600
pen to do it.

43:55.920 --> 43:56.220
Right.

43:56.640 --> 43:57.660
You pay the penalty of

43:57.660 --> 43:58.700
losing distinctness.

43:58.900 --> 44:00.020
But it is a simple

44:00.020 --> 44:01.320
symmetrical rollback.

44:01.460 --> 44:02.680
You delete the item from

44:02.680 --> 44:03.320
the inventory.

44:03.760 --> 44:05.140
The generative machinery of

44:05.140 --> 44:06.500
the alphabet doesn't break

44:06.500 --> 44:07.880
if you stop drawing dots.

44:08.000 --> 44:08.900
It just gets a lot harder

44:08.900 --> 44:09.380
to read.

44:09.660 --> 44:11.000
Now, contrast that with a

44:11.000 --> 44:11.800
depth one reversal.

44:12.660 --> 44:14.300
What if a society wanted to

44:14.300 --> 44:15.580
undo positional

44:15.580 --> 44:16.340
regularization?

44:16.920 --> 44:17.940
What if they wanted to

44:17.940 --> 44:19.240
abandon the clean

44:19.240 --> 44:20.680
four-position system

44:20.680 --> 44:22.520
and regress to the fully

44:22.520 --> 44:24.640
context-sensitive ligatures

44:24.640 --> 44:26.160
where every letter connects

44:26.160 --> 44:27.380
uniquely based on its

44:27.380 --> 44:27.660
neighbors?

44:28.100 --> 44:29.240
Well, you aren't just paying

44:29.240 --> 44:31.060
a higher distinctness cost

44:31.060 --> 44:32.120
on the balance sheet at that

44:32.120 --> 44:32.320
point.

44:32.380 --> 44:32.680
No.

44:33.200 --> 44:34.180
You would literally have to

44:34.180 --> 44:35.720
re-derive or completely

44:35.720 --> 44:37.560
reinvent the entire lost

44:37.560 --> 44:38.680
combinatorial mapping.

44:39.040 --> 44:40.440
You have to resurrect the

44:40.440 --> 44:42.040
complex mathematical function

44:42.040 --> 44:44.180
of f given g sub i minus

44:44.180 --> 44:46.080
one and g sub i plus one that

44:46.080 --> 44:46.980
the culture destroyed

44:46.980 --> 44:47.980
centuries ago.

44:48.200 --> 44:48.580
Wow.

44:48.960 --> 44:50.140
It is the difference between

44:50.140 --> 44:51.500
deleting a paragraph from a

44:51.500 --> 44:53.500
book versus deleting the

44:53.500 --> 44:54.980
foundational rules of grammar

44:54.980 --> 44:56.120
for the language that book

44:56.120 --> 44:56.620
is written in.

44:56.680 --> 44:57.660
That's a powerful way to

44:57.660 --> 44:58.020
frame it.

44:58.280 --> 44:58.880
Think about it.

44:58.980 --> 45:00.400
If I accidentally delete a

45:00.400 --> 45:01.680
paragraph from my Word document,

45:02.020 --> 45:03.140
I could just rewrite it from

45:03.140 --> 45:03.500
memory.

45:03.780 --> 45:04.320
It's annoying.

45:04.460 --> 45:05.200
It costs me time.

45:05.200 --> 45:06.540
But it's a linear,

45:06.800 --> 45:07.760
straightforward cost.

45:08.220 --> 45:09.900
But if I somehow uninvented

45:09.900 --> 45:11.380
the concept of syntax or the

45:11.380 --> 45:13.060
concept of verbs entirely, I

45:13.060 --> 45:14.980
can't just undo that loss.

45:15.260 --> 45:16.780
I have to rebuild the human

45:16.780 --> 45:18.940
cognitive capacity to structure

45:18.940 --> 45:21.020
thought from absolute scratch.

45:21.400 --> 45:21.900
Exactly.

45:22.280 --> 45:24.000
A depth one change burns the

45:24.000 --> 45:24.820
bridge behind it.

45:25.220 --> 45:26.700
The flat embodied constraint

45:26.700 --> 45:28.060
model noticed that the script

45:28.060 --> 45:29.300
got simpler over time.

45:29.640 --> 45:30.820
It accurately measured the

45:30.820 --> 45:32.100
entropy reduction from an

45:32.100 --> 45:34.040
unbounded matrix to a clean

45:34.040 --> 45:35.200
four position system.

45:35.600 --> 45:36.640
But because its mathematical

45:36.640 --> 45:38.180
formula lacked a depth

45:38.180 --> 45:39.940
variable, it couldn't explain

45:39.940 --> 45:41.480
why the script never smoothly

45:41.480 --> 45:42.960
slid backward when economic

45:42.960 --> 45:43.840
pressures change.

45:43.920 --> 45:44.620
It couldn't see the

45:44.620 --> 45:45.380
irreversibility.

45:45.720 --> 45:46.860
The cost of a depth one

45:46.860 --> 45:48.400
reversal is not simply the

45:48.400 --> 45:49.580
sum total of a thousand

45:49.580 --> 45:50.560
depth zero changes.

45:50.820 --> 45:52.100
It is a qualitatively different

45:52.100 --> 45:53.860
category of cost entirely.

45:54.480 --> 45:55.820
It is the cost of restoring

45:55.820 --> 45:57.200
lost generative machinery.

45:57.900 --> 45:59.460
Once the collective memory of

45:59.460 --> 46:00.940
the old rule is gone, the

46:00.940 --> 46:02.240
system is permanently locked

46:02.240 --> 46:03.360
into its new reality.

46:03.360 --> 46:04.940
Let's synthesize the journey

46:04.940 --> 46:06.080
we've been on today because

46:06.080 --> 46:07.220
Flyxion has given us an

46:07.220 --> 46:08.800
incredibly powerful lens here.

46:09.340 --> 46:10.960
We started by asking why

46:10.960 --> 46:12.360
complex systems stabilize.

46:13.180 --> 46:14.440
And we've discovered that a

46:14.440 --> 46:16.320
writing system, or really any

46:16.320 --> 46:18.480
complex architecture, isn't just

46:18.480 --> 46:19.900
a flat collection of features

46:19.900 --> 46:22.440
evaluated on a simple cost-benefit

46:22.440 --> 46:22.900
spreadsheet.

46:23.700 --> 46:25.060
It is a deeply layered

46:25.060 --> 46:25.800
architecture.

46:25.960 --> 46:26.820
It's all about depth.

46:27.160 --> 46:27.420
Right.

46:27.900 --> 46:29.780
Modifying the surface, like adding

46:29.780 --> 46:31.580
a dot to a letter, stamping a new

46:31.580 --> 46:33.620
cookie from a mold, executing a

46:33.620 --> 46:35.000
known grammatical rule at depth

46:35.000 --> 46:36.400
zero that gives a system

46:36.400 --> 46:38.060
predictability, speed, and

46:38.060 --> 46:38.800
immediate clarity.

46:39.420 --> 46:40.800
But modifying the generative

46:40.800 --> 46:42.740
machinery itself, like destroying

46:42.740 --> 46:44.560
the context-sensitive ligatures and

46:44.560 --> 46:45.960
inventing the four-position rule,

46:46.380 --> 46:48.520
or historically fixing the ten forms

46:48.520 --> 46:50.620
of verbs at depth one that defines

46:50.620 --> 46:52.500
the entire future trajectory of the

46:52.500 --> 46:52.800
system.

46:52.800 --> 46:54.340
And it makes going backward nearly

46:54.340 --> 46:55.480
mathematically impossible.

46:55.640 --> 46:55.960
Exactly.

46:55.960 --> 46:58.020
And this framework forces us to ask

46:58.020 --> 46:59.680
very pointed, very uncomfortable

46:59.680 --> 47:01.360
questions about the complex systems

47:01.360 --> 47:03.220
we interact with every single day.

47:03.520 --> 47:04.720
I was hoping we'd get to this.

47:04.920 --> 47:06.440
Because when you consider your own

47:06.440 --> 47:07.800
work, the structure of your

47:07.800 --> 47:09.620
business, your daily behavioral

47:09.620 --> 47:11.540
habits, or even the code you write

47:11.540 --> 47:13.420
for a project, you have to ask

47:13.420 --> 47:15.380
yourself, when I am trying to solve

47:15.380 --> 47:17.520
a persistent problem, am I just

47:17.520 --> 47:18.440
adding a dot?

47:18.540 --> 47:20.120
Am I just tweaking the surface?

47:20.440 --> 47:23.000
Am I just making a depth zero tweak

47:23.000 --> 47:24.020
to the surface output?

47:24.620 --> 47:26.460
Or am I actually doing the hard,

47:26.620 --> 47:28.500
irreversible work of engaging with

47:28.500 --> 47:30.180
the generative rules of my behavior

47:30.180 --> 47:31.440
at depth one?

47:32.040 --> 47:33.580
Recognizing the difference can save

47:33.580 --> 47:35.180
you from the endless exhausting

47:35.180 --> 47:37.260
frustration of trying to fix a rule

47:37.260 --> 47:39.060
level structural problem with a

47:39.060 --> 47:39.980
surface level tool.

47:40.160 --> 47:40.340
Yeah.

47:40.480 --> 47:42.160
I mean, you can dot letters all day

47:42.160 --> 47:43.460
long to try and make things clearer,

47:43.620 --> 47:45.300
but if the underlying joining rules

47:45.300 --> 47:47.360
of the script are broken, the system

47:47.360 --> 47:49.060
will fundamentally continue to fail.

47:49.220 --> 47:50.320
It's a profound realization.

47:50.780 --> 47:52.740
Which leaves us with a final, somewhat

47:52.740 --> 47:54.260
provocative thought to ponder,

47:54.740 --> 47:56.060
beating directly on what Flyxion

47:56.060 --> 47:57.120
has shown us about the

47:57.120 --> 47:58.140
architecture of language.

47:58.580 --> 48:00.360
We just spent this entire deep dive

48:00.360 --> 48:01.960
exploring how human language

48:01.960 --> 48:04.500
stabilized itself by taking its most

48:04.500 --> 48:06.720
fundamental generative rules and

48:06.720 --> 48:08.140
locking them down at depth one.

48:08.660 --> 48:11.040
By making those rules visible, fixed,

48:11.180 --> 48:13.000
and highly teachable, humanity

48:13.000 --> 48:15.200
achieved the miracle of predictive

48:15.200 --> 48:15.880
generativity.

48:16.580 --> 48:18.660
We know exactly how a word is formed,

48:18.860 --> 48:20.680
and we know exactly what it costs

48:20.680 --> 48:21.440
to change it.

48:21.440 --> 48:22.640
We can see the rules.

48:22.760 --> 48:24.080
But what happens to human thought

48:24.080 --> 48:25.660
and the stability of our complex

48:25.660 --> 48:28.260
systems when we increasingly rely on

48:28.260 --> 48:30.020
artificial intelligence models where

48:30.020 --> 48:31.720
the generative rules are not fixed,

48:32.160 --> 48:33.280
teachable grammar tables?

48:33.780 --> 48:34.980
What happens when the generative

48:34.980 --> 48:36.620
machinery of our communication is

48:36.620 --> 48:39.140
completely hidden inside billions of

48:39.140 --> 48:40.940
opaque weights within a black box?

48:41.100 --> 48:42.660
It is a profound structural

48:42.660 --> 48:43.220
vulnerability.

48:43.960 --> 48:45.720
If the machinery operating at depth one

48:45.720 --> 48:47.620
is permanently invisible to the user,

48:47.940 --> 48:49.820
we lose the cognitive ability to

48:49.820 --> 48:51.420
differentiate it from a simple

48:51.420 --> 48:53.320
depth zero execution.

48:53.980 --> 48:55.720
And if we can't see the depth of the

48:55.720 --> 48:59.320
rule, how will we ever know what is

48:59.320 --> 49:00.740
going to cost us to change it?

49:01.520 --> 49:03.460
How will we know if a shift in the

49:03.460 --> 49:05.700
model's behavior can ever be reversed at

49:05.700 --> 49:06.020
all?

49:06.720 --> 49:08.820
It is something to deeply consider the

49:08.820 --> 49:10.340
next time you ask a machine to

49:10.340 --> 49:11.780
generate a block of text for you.

49:12.320 --> 49:14.600
Are you simply using a tool to change a

49:14.600 --> 49:14.940
document?

49:14.940 --> 49:17.580
Or is the machine subtly rewriting the

49:17.580 --> 49:19.160
invisible operating system of how you

49:19.160 --> 49:19.640
communicate?

49:20.400 --> 49:22.340
A very unsettling question to leave on.

49:22.460 --> 49:24.000
Well, thank you so much for joining us on

49:24.000 --> 49:25.900
this custom deep dive into the source

49:25.900 --> 49:26.300
material.

49:26.800 --> 49:28.420
We hope this exploration of depth,

49:28.860 --> 49:30.640
rules, and stabilization gave you a

49:30.640 --> 49:32.500
powerful new framework for looking at

49:32.500 --> 49:32.840
the world.

49:33.060 --> 49:33.760
Thank you for listening.

